1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dadildis_de_Pallars
2 CONT
2 CONT ============================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents unknown, but often said to have been a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Lope-IV-Count-Of-Bigorre/6000000000437081406 Lope IV de Bigorre] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Faquil%C3%A8ne-de-Toulouse/6000000000424707234
2 CONC  Faquilène de Rouergue].
2 CONT
2 CONT The Codex de Roda records that "Garsea Scemenonis" married secondly "domna Dadildi de Paliares soror Regimundi comitis"[193].
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Søster til: Raimund I Count of Pallars and Ribagorza, der også hører til mine aner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leo: Europäische Stammtafeln, J.A. Stargardt Verlag, Marburg, Schwennicke, Detlev (Ed.), Reference: II 54.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garc%C3%ADa_Jiménez_de_Pamplona '''García Jiménez'''] (835-after 885) was a high-medieval knight of the realm of Pamplona, who is mentioned by that surname in the Codex of Roda. He was co-regent of t
2 CONC he kingdom during the reigns of García Íñiguez of Pamplona and his son Fortún Garcés.a
2 CONT .
2 CONT
2 CONT The Códice de Roda shows García Jiménez to have married twice, firstly to Oneca, "Rebel of Sangüesa" with whom he had two children:
2 CONT # Íñigo, called 'king' in the Códice de Roda when reporting his marriage to a granddaughter of Fortún Garcés of Pamplona, but not in his own entry as son of García Jiménez. He perhaps succeeded to his father's sub-kingdom (else th
2 CONC e term is being used as an honorific rather than a title).
2 CONT # Sancha, married as her first husband Íñigo Fortúnez, son of king Fortún Garcés of Pamplona, and subsequently remarried to Galindo Aznárez II, Count of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT García Jiménez married secondly''' Dadildis de Pallars''', sister of count Raymond I of Pallars and Ribagorza, having by her two sons:
2 CONT # Sancho I, later sole king of Pamplona.
2 CONT # Jimeno, tutor of his nephew García Sánchez and regent until his death on 29 May 931.
2 CONT
2 CONT
