1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho_I_of_Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Garcés I (Basque: Antso Ia. Gartzez; c. 860 – 10 December 925),[1] also known as Sancho I, was king of Pamplona from 905 until 925. He was the son of García Jiménez and was the first king of Pamplona of the Jiménez dynasty.
2 CONC [2] Sancho I was the feudal ruler of the Onsella valley, and expanded his power to all the neighboring territories. He was chosen to replace Fortún Garcés by the Pamplonese nobility in 905.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Garcés was born around the year 860, son of García Jiménez and his second wife Dadildis de Pallars.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Король Наварры, первый представитель наваррской королевской династии Хименесов и первый из правителей королевства Наварра, который вёл завоевательную политику по отношению к соседним мусульманским владениям.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.biografiasyvidas.com/biografia/s/sancho_i_garces.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho_Garc%C3%A9s_I_de_Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Garcés I (n.Sangüesa (actual Rocaforte) 865 - † Resa, 10 de diciembre de 925). Rey de Pamplona entre los años 905 y 925.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hijo de García Jiménez, descendiente de la dinastía Jimena. A la muerte de García I Íñiguez en el año 870, es gobernante de la Valdonsella y pronto comienza a intervenir en todos los territorios circundantes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ocupa Pamplona cuando todavía reina Fortún Garcés, ayudado por Alfonso III de Asturias, junto con el conde de Pallars. Eliminados los derechos patrimoniales de los hijos de Fortún Garcés, estos recaerán en su nieta Toda, casada co
2 CONC n Sancho Garcés I, que los hizo valer y se proclamó rey de Pamplona en 905, tras destronar a Fortún Garcés.
2 CONT
2 CONT Al morir el conde de Aragón Galindo Aznárez II, Sancho Garcés I ocupó las tierras de Aragón ignorando los derechos sucesorios de todos. Ésta fue la causa que justificó las luchas del gobernador musulmán de Huesca, al-Tawil, que te
2 CONC nía derechos sucesorios sobre el territorio por estar casado con Sancha, hermana del conde. Se solucionó el problema al prometer en matrimonio a Andregoto Galíndez, hija de Galindo Aznárez II, con el hijo de Sancho Garcés I, el fu
2 CONC turo rey García Sánchez I, que era todavía un niño.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amplió considerablemente las fronteras meridionales del reino hasta llegar a tierras riojanas mediante una serie de campañas militares contra los musulmanes. Conquistó Nájera y estableció allí su corte, dotando de una organización
2 CONC  definitiva al reino de Pamplona.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aliado con Ordoño II de León, venció a un ejército cordobés en San Esteban de Gormaz (917), pero fue derrotado por Abd al-Rahman III en Valdejunquera (920).
2 CONT
2 CONT Durante su reinado se comienza a acuñar moneda, siendo el primer reino cristiano que use tal regalía. Así mismo, aparece el sistema de tenencias, que se perpetuará en Navarra y Aragón hasta principios del siglo XIII.
2 CONT
2 CONT El centro político del mundo cristiano estaba en la corte de Nájera que dio como resultado varios matrimonios reales de las hijas de Sancho Garcés I y la reina Toda Aznar:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Urraca de Pamplona, casada con Ramiro II de León.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Oneca de Pamplona, casada con Alfonso IV "El Monje" de León. Fue reina de León entre 926 y 931. Murió en 931.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sancha de Pamplona, casada en primeras nupcias con Ordoño II de León, en segundas con el Conde alavés Álvaro Herrameliz y en terceras, con Fernán González, Conde de Castilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * García I Sánchez, Rey de Pamplona, casado con Andregoto Galíndez y con Teresa de León.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Velasquita o Belasquita Sánchez, casada en primeras nupcias con el Conde alaves Munio Velaz, en segundas con Galindo de Ribagorza y en terceras con Fortún Galíndez.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Munia (Muña) de Pamplona, casada con Ordoño I de Asturias.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Orbita de Navarra, probablemente casada con al-Tawil, gobernador de Huesca. Pudo ser hija póstuma, como hace suponer el significado de su nombre, "la huérfana".
2 CONT
2 CONT El rey Sancho Garcés I murió en las cercanías de Resa, a orillas del río Ebro, el día 10 de diciembre del año 925 y fue enterrado en San Esteban de Deio en Monjardín.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho I Garcés (c. 860 – December 11, 925) was king of Pamplona from 905 to 925. He was a son of García Jiménez, who was regent of Pamplona from 870 to 880 while Fortún Garcés was held captive and apparently co-king of Pamplona f
2 CONC rom 860 to his death in 882, and Dadildis de Pallars. Sancho may also have been a co-king during the reign of Fortún. The elderly Sancho (already 45 years old) succeeded King Fortún when the latter was deposed by a coalition of en
2 CONC emies: the Banu Qasi under Lope ibn Mohammed, King Alfonso III of Asturias, and Sancho's uncle, the count of Pallars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho's first wife Urraca, daughter of the count of Aragón, did not have surviving children. So Sancho married a second time to Toda Aznárez in his old age. His children were thus minors upon his death. Queen Toda (born Teuda de 
2 CONC Larraun) was a daughter of Aznar Sánchez, lord of Larraun, and Oneca Fortúnez, who herself was a daughter of King Fortún. Thus, Toda's children were also descendants of the Arista dynasty of Navarrese monarchs. Sancho fought again
2 CONC st the Moors with repeated success and joined Ultra-Puertos, or Basse-Navarre (Baja Navarra), to his own dominions, also extending his territory as far as Nájera. As a thanksgiving offering for his victories, he founded, in 924, t
2 CONC he convent of Albelda. Before his death, all the Moors had been driven from the country.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho was succeeded by his son García Sánchez, with his widow Toda and brother Jimeno (who used the royal title) acting as regents.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Codex of Roda gives Sancho and Toda six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Oneca (d.931), married Alfonso IV the Monk of León in 926
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sancha, married firstly Ordoño II of León, secondly Count Alvaro Herraméliz of Álava, and thirdly Fernán González, Count of Castile
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Urraca, married Ramiro II of León
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Velasquita (or Belasquita), married firstly Munio, count of Vizcaya, secondly Galindo, son of Bernard count of Ribagorza.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Orbita
2 CONT
2 CONT     * García, king of Pamplona, married firstly Andregota Galíndez and secondly Teresa
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho also had an illegitimate daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lupa, mother of Raymond I, Count of Bigorre
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho I Garcés (c. 860 – December 11, 925) was king of Pamplona from 905 to 925. He was a son of García Jiménez, who was king of "another part of the kingdom" of Pamplona and Dadildis de Pallars, his second wife. In 905, a coalit
2 CONC ion of enemies of the king, Fortún Garcés: Lubb ibn Muhammed of the Banu Qasi, King Alfonso III of Asturias, Galindo Aznar II of Aragon and Sancho's uncle, Raymond I of Pallars and Ribagorza, deposed the king, and put Sancho on th
2 CONC e throne in his place. Throughout his reign, he involved himself in the squabbles among the Muslim lords to the south with repeated success. In 907, he turned on his former ally Lubb ibn Muhammad, killing him in battle. Four years
2 CONC  later, another former ally, Galindo Aznar, joined with his brother-in-law Muhammad al-Tawil and Abd Allah ibn Lubb ibn Qasi to attack Sancho, but they were crushed: al-Tawil was killed, the power of the Banu Qasi was severely cri
2 CONC ppled, and Galindo forced into vassalage to Sancho, leading to the incorporation of the County of Aragon into Pamplona. In 920, he teamed with Bernard I of Ribagorza and Amrus ibn Muhammed, son of Muhammad al-Tawil, to attack Monz
2 CONC ón. He joined Ultra-Puertos, or Basse-Navarre (Baja Navarra), to his own dominions, also extending his territory as far as Nájera. As a thanksgiving offering for his victories, he founded, in 924, the convent of Albelda.
2 CONT
2 CONT [source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancho_I_of_Pamplona]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
