2 NOTE yes well thanks,  just one thing after a year:  Let me remove the TAG from the profile. 
3 CONT
3 CONT JPGs can be moved to the main without removing the others, and anyone who turns the Middle Ages into this level of detail should master it, otherwise it's dangerous to let them modify the Middle Ages!  
3 CONT
3 CONT Why do I want  the profile to remain on the list until I've checked it too? Because some of the least suited to medieval modifications have attached to my ankles: They take you literally, like a child trying to make fun of you. Yo
3 CONC u're too good to punish them; I suffer from too many persecution crazes to ignore their childish actions :D  
2 NOTE Thanks for the attractive image, Livio, and the work finding profiles it’s tagged to.
3 CONT
3 CONT The books (without specifics) represent that the profile is known to history, and described in publications and encyclopedias; but does not yet have a specific, copyright-free image uploaded to geni.  So, we are prompted to enhanc
3 CONC e the profile another step: find a correct coat of arms, for example.  Then the “in books” image can be de-tagged from profile. 
