1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fredelon, Freddon, or Fredol (died 852) was the first Count of Toulouse (844 – 852) of the dynasty of Rouergue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Fulcoald of Rouergue and Senegund, daughter of Alda, sister of William of Gellone, Fredeon was related to the families of the counts of Rouergue and Toulouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 840, Fulcoald died, but Fredelon was not confirmed as his successor in Rouergue. But when Bernard of Septimania was captured by Charles the Bald for rebellion against his lord and executed in 844, the king bestowed his county o
2 CONC f Toulouse on Fredelon. Pepin II of Aquitaine, who was leading the revolt against Charles, appointed Bernard's heir William to the county of Toulouse. Of the two claimants to Toulouse, William had the upper hand. In 849, however, 
2 CONC William was in Barcelona and Charles invaded Aquitaine. Fredelon, then in control of Toulouse, taking advantage of William's absence, opened the gates of the city to his sovereign and was reconfirmed in his possession of it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fredelon received the County of Carcassonne in 850 and died in 852, leaving his titles to his brother Raymond. By his wife Oda, he left one daughter named Udalgarda who married Bernard Plantapilosa.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fredelon_of_Toulouse
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT FREDELON ([815]-[849/52]).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 3 Nov 862 under which "Raymundus…comes et marchio et uxor mea Berteyz" founded the abbey of Vabres for the souls of "genitoris nostri Fulgualdi et…genetri
2 CONC ce mea Senegundi et…germano meo Fredolone quondam"[188].  He took part in the recapture of Toulouse by Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks from Pepin II King of Aquitaine in 845.  The king appointed Fredelon as Governor
2 CONC  of Toulouse [850]-[852] and he used the title “Custos Civitatis” of Toulouse.  m ---.  The name of Fredelon's wife is not known.  Fredelon & his wife had [one possible child]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         [FULCRADE ([840]-after 878).  Settipani suggests that she may have been the daughter of Fredelon, and also speculates on her possible descendants[189].  He bases this on the charter dated Mar 924 under which "Senegundis
2 CONC " donated property to Conques for the souls of "filio meo Fredolone et…genitori meo Warmario et genetrice mea Folcradanæ…viro meo Amblardo sive Jorio et…filiorum meorum Stephano, Bernardo, Adalgario sive Jorio"[190].  m GARNIER, s
2 CONC on of RAINAUD & his wife ---.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE.htm
