1 NAME García el Malo Galíndez, conde de Aragón
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 833
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Se casó con Matrona, hija de Aznar I Galíndez conde de Aragón. Mató a su cuñado Centulfo y repudió a Matrona para casarse con Nunila de Pamplona, hija de Íñigo Arista rey de Pamplona, con la que tuvo un hijo, Galin
2 CONC do Garcés.
2 CONT ===========================
2 CONT
2 CONT García I Galíndez «el Malo» (m. 833), conde de Aragón (820-833). Las pocas noticias sobre su vida, recogidas por historiadores posteriores, se encuentran en el Códice de Roda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hijo de Galindo Belascotenes y de Faquilo
2 CONT -----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT García Galíndez (died 833), called the Bad (el Malo), was the Count of Aragon and Conflent from 820.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Galindo Belascotenes, he married Matrona, daughter of Aznar Galíndez I. He later murdered his brother-in-law Centule and repudiated Matrona to marry Nunila, daughter of Íñigo Arista of Pamplona. According to tradition, whic
2 CONC h bestowed upon García his nickname, he murdered his brother-in-law for a joke that he and Galindo Aznárez I had played on him, namely, locking him up in a house during the Hogueras de San Juan.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 820, Íñigo gathered a small army and deposed Aznar from Aragon and his other counties, bestowing them on García. In 824, when Aeblus and Aznar Sánchez marched on Pamplona, García and Musa ibn Fortún of the Banu Qasi lent their 
2 CONC support to Íñigo and the Frankish counts were defeated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Depending on the source, he either died in 833 or just retired, leaving the government to his son Galindo Garcés.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Collins, Roger. The Basques. Blackwell Publishing: London, 1990.
2 CONT
2 CONT Higounet, Charles. Bordeaux pendant le haut moyen age. Bordeaux, 1963.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis, Archibald R. The Development of Southern French and Catalan Society, 718–1050. University of Texas Press: Austin, 1965.
2 CONT
2 CONT Foundation for Medieval Genealogy: Aragon.
