1 NOTE Count of Meark. Founder of the Banu Qasi. He was born a Visigoth and converted to Muhammedanism in the year 0714. When Musa ben Nusier al Bekir occupied the Ebro Valley during the Moorish invasion Cassius, a smart politico pragmat
2 CONC ically converted to Islam. This was done with the intent of retaining power, at least locally. He managed to protect the Asturian part of the Visigothic kingdom. Musa ibn Fortun founded half of what became the kingdom of Navarre, 
2 CONC whose regents, the Banu Qasi were related. It kept its independence through the art of diplomacy and military alliances both with the Basques who still regard Navarre as theirs and with the Mosarabs (non converted Christians of th
2 CONC e Moors).
2 CONT Musa ibn Fortun was called the third king of Espagna and his son, Lope ibn Musa was installed as Consul of Toledo. It all collapsed in 859 at Clavijo when Ordono I attacked and defeated Musa ibn Fortun in battle. Musa ibn Fortun s
2 CONC eems always to have regarded himself as a Goth but his mother was a descendant of the Prophet Mohammed. (Sunni Scholars).
