1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====The name of Hugues' wife is without a primary source.
2 CONT * Webpage "Our Royal Titled Noble and Commoner Ancestors and Cousins" names [https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p339.htm#i10167 Hugh I, Comte de Quercy, Comborn] and defers to ''Europaische Stammtafeln'' by 
2 CONC Isenburg, chart 763, 765 and ''Généalogie Famille de Carné'' by naming "Gudinilda" as Hugues' wife. Only with subscription access to these pedigrees can one see if there is a source citation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulcentw.htm#HuguesRouergeuQuercydied972B Toulouse, Central & Western]
2 CONT * [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulcentw.htm#HuguesRouergeuQuercydied972B '''HUGUES de Rouergue'''], son of ERMENGAUD Comte de Rouergue & his wife Adelais —— (-[after 972]). "''Ermengaudus comes et filius suus Regimundus et R
2 CONC ainus vicecomes et vicarius''" donated property "''in pago Ruthenico in ministerio Curiense in villa…Seviniaco''" to Vabres by charter dated Jan [934], subscribed by "…''Ugone filio Ermengaudo, Bernardo vicecomite, Ildoino, Adalon
2 CONC e''"[559]. '''Comte''' ['''de Quercy''']. "…''Domni Pontii ducis Aquitanorum et comitis Tolosani, Guarsindis uxoris eius, Hugonis comitis, Arnaudi vicecomitis, Sicardi vicecomitis, Atonis, Pontii''" signed the charter dated Aug 94
2 CONC 0 under which Aimery Archbishop of Narbonne and Rodoald Bishop of Béziers donated property to Saint-Pons de Thomières[560]. "''Atto…vicecomes''" donated property to Saint-Pons de Thomières, on the advice of "''uxoris meæ''", for t
2 CONC he souls of "''patris mei Bernardi et matris meæ''" by charter dated Apr 942, subscribed by "''Frotarius episcopus, Bernardus, Hugonis comitis, Dagberga''…"[561]. The testament of "''Gersindæ comitissæ''", dated to [972], bequeath
2 CONC ed property for life "''ecclesiam…Sancti Symphoriani cum alode…Cabannes excepto Dauker''" to "''Ugoni comiti nepoti me''o"[562]. No Comte Hugues has been identified at the time except for the brother of Raymond [I] Comte de Rouerg
2 CONC ue, although no other indication has yet been found that he was still alive at the date of this testament. If the co-identity is correct, the precise relationship between him and Gersendis Ctss de Toulouse has not yet been ascerta
2 CONC ined. '''Vicomte de Comborn'''.  
2 CONT * '''m ——.'''  The name of Hugues´s wife is not known. Hugues & his wife had [two] children: 
2 CONT ** 1. [ARCHAMBAUD "Camba-Putrida/Jambe-Pourrie" (-[1000] or after). According to ''Europäische Stammtafeln''[563], Archambaud Vicomte de Comborn was the possible son of Hugues Comte de Quercy, Vicomte de Comborn, presumably based 
2 CONC on his succession to his supposed father at Comborn. Vicomte de Comborn 962.  —  VICOMTES de COMBORN.] 
2 CONT ** 2. BERNARD. The ''Vita Sancti Abbonis'' names "''Bernardum pater Hugo''" when recording his appointment as abbé de Solignac[564].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Medlands does not include a Gudinilda as dau. of [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CATALAN%20NOBILITY.htm#SunyerIBarcelonadied950B Sunyer I de Barcelona]:
2 CONT * SUNYER [I] de Barcelona, son of GUIFRÉ [I] "el Velloso/el Pilós/the Hairy" Comte de Barcelona & his wife Guinidilda --- (-15 Oct 954, bur Ripoll Monastery)....'''m''' (917 or before) '''RICHILDE''', daughter of --- (-after 954).
2 CONC ...Szabolcs de Vajay suggests[188] that she was Richilde de Rouergue, daughter of Ermengaud de Toulouse Comte de Rouergue & his wife Adelais ---, to explain the transmission of the name Armengol [Ermengaud] into the Barcelona fami
2 CONC ly. 
2 CONT * Sunyer [I] & his wife had five children:
2 CONT ** 1. BORRELL [II] (-30 Sep 993)....''et cetera''
2 CONT ** 2. ARMENGOL (-21 Aug [940/942])....''et cetera''
2 CONT ** 3. MIRÓ (-31 Oct 966)....''et cetera''
2 CONT ** 4.  ADELAIDA [Bonafilia] (-[after 11 Mar 988])....''et cetera''
2 CONT ** 5. JOZFREDO (-after 25 Mar 988)....''et cetera''
2 CONT
2 CONT ====es.Wikipedia''' does not name a Gudinilda as dau. of [https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suniario_de_Barcelona Suniario de Barcelona], and neither does [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suniaire_Ier_de_Barcelone fr.Wikipedia], [https:
2 CONC //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunyer,_Count_of_Barcelona en.Wikipedia], nor [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunyer_I._(Barcelona) de.Wikipedia].
