1 NOTE Jimeno Sanches El Fuerte: brings us more controversy. This time it has to do with his name,
2 CONT El Fuerte. If you speak and read and write Spanish you know that El Fuerte means, "The Strong" or one who is strong. But again, historians like to waste a lot of their time because some say "El Fuerte" translates into "The Cruel".
2 CONC  You make your own choice.
2 CONT Some more history: The Romans tried to conquer the Basques, they couldn't so they  were forced to trade with them.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Romans show up in the year 75 BC and they established Pamplona which was named after Pompey the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimeno also goes by the name, Ximeno. I place him as being the founder of the Jimenez line.
2 CONT According to relationship caculator he is my 34th great grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Soruce: Codex de Roda
2 CONT Ayes.
