1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2.         ADALRIC (-before 814).  [Duke of Gascony.]  The Vita Hludowici Imperatoris records that "Chorso dux Tholosanus" was defeated by "cuiusdam Wasconis, Adelerici" by forces of Charles I King of the Franks an
2 CONC d exiled, but later killed in battle[23]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adalric_of_Gascony
2 CONT
2 CONT Adalric was probably a Basque[1] lord in the late eighth century in Gascony. He has been called a possible Duke of Gascony by some scholars.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a possible son of Lupo II of Gascony. After Lupo's death, Adalric controlled western Gascony including Lower Navarre, Béarn, and Bigorre.[2] His brother Sancho controlled the east.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the spurious Charte d'Alaon, Adalric was captured by forces of Charlemagne and exiled to Spain, later being killed in battle.[3] This charter also makes him the father of Seguin I of Bordeaux and Centule. His relation
2 CONC ships are, in fact, unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/GASCONY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT LOUP, son of [HATTO & his wife Vandrade ---] (-murdered [775]). The charter of Charles II "le Chauve" King of the West Franks dated 30 Jan 845 (probably spurious, as explained in the Introduction) names "Lupo Duci" as son of "Hatt
2 CONC onis Ducis"[5]. His parentage has not been corroborated by other primary sources consulted. m ---. The name of Loup's wife is not known.  Loup & his wife had [three] children:
2 CONT *1. [ADALRIC . The name of Adalric's wife is not known. Adalric & his wife had [two] children:] ...
2 CONT **a)         [JIMENO (-after [814/15]). m ---.  The name of Jimeno's wife is not known.  Jimeno & his wife had one child:]
2 CONT **b)         [CENTULE (-[812]). The name of Centule's wife is not known.  Centule & his wife had [two] children:]
