1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ermesinda_of_Bigorre
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermesinda of Bigorre (Aragonese: Ermisenda de Bigorra), born Gerberga or Gisberga (1015 – 1 December 1049), was a Queen of Aragon, a daughter of Bernard-Roger, Count of Bigorre and his wife Garsenda, Heiress of Bigorre. She was a 
2 CONC member of the House of Foix, the sister of Bernard II, Count of Bigorre, Roger I, Count of Foix, and perhaps of Stephanie who married García Sánchez III of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerberga married on 22 August 1036 to King Ramiro I of Aragon. After her wedding Gerberga changed her name to Ermesinda. The couple were married for thirteen years, in which time her husband elevated himself from a vassal holding 
2 CONC scattered lands around Jaca into a de facto ruler of pocket-kingdom spanning the former counties of Aragon, Sobrarbe and Ribagorza, and is thereby credited with being the first King of Aragon. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho Ramírez (c. 1042 – 4 June 1094), succeeded his father. García, Bishop of Jaca (d. 17 July 1086) Teresa (b. 1037), married William Bertrand of Provence, no issue. Sancha (d. 1097), possibly married firstly to Pons, Count of 
2 CONC Toulouse, and secondly to Ermengol III, Count of Urgell Urraca (d. 1077), a nun.
2 CONT
2 CONT All of Ermesinda's children lived to adulthood. She died on 1 December 1049 and she was buried at the Monastery of San Juan de la Peña.[5] Her husband remarried four years later to Agnes.http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?person
2 CONC ID=I00093519&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================
2 CONT Gisberga fue la primera reina de Aragón, esposa de Ramiro I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Era hija de Bernardo Roger de Foix, conde de Foix, y al contraer matrimonio cambió su su nombre por Ermesinda. Gobernó el reino a la muerte de su esposo, que pereció en una batalla en 1063 y compartió después el poder con su hijo 
2 CONC Sancho. Fue enterrada el monasterio de San Juan de la Peña.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilberga de Couserans1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 1016, d. 1054
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Bernard Roger I, comte de Couserans, de Foix et de Bigorre b. circa 990, d. circa 1038
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Gersinde, comtesse de Bigorre b. circa 995, d. after 1038
2 CONT
2 CONT      Also called Gisberga of Bigorre.2 Also called Hermesenda. Gilberga de Couserans was the daughter of Bernardo Roger, count of Couserans, and Garsenda, countess of Bigorre.1 She was born circa 1016. She was the daughter of Bern
2 CONC ard Roger I, comte de Couserans, de Foix et de Bigorre and Gersinde, comtesse de Bigorre. Gilberga de Couserans married Ramiro I, rey de Aragón, son of Sancho III "el Mayor", rey de Pamplona y conde de Aragón and Sancha Garcia de 
2 CONC Aybar, on 22 August 1036 at Jaca, Huesca Province, Aragón, Spain.2,1 Gilberga de Couserans died in 1054.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro I, rey de Aragón b. circa 1015?, d. 8 May 1063
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
