1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo Aznárez II (died 922) was Count of Aragon from 893 to 922. He was the son of Aznar Galíndez II and his wife Onneca Garcés, daughter of King García Íñiguez of Pamplona.[1]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo was married twice. By his first wife, Acibella,[2] daughter of Count García II Sánchez of Gascony,[3] and his wife Amuna of Périgord, he had three children:
2 CONT # Toda Galíndez, married to Bernat I, Count of Ribagorza,[4] to whom she brought Sobrarbe.
2 CONT # Redemptus Galíndez, bishop.[3]
2 CONT # Mirón Galíndez,[3] who probably died before his father since he did not inherit the county in spite of being a legitimate son
2 CONT
2 CONT By his second wife, Sancha Garcés of Pamplona, daughter of García Jiménez and Onneca Rebelle of Sangüesa, and half-sister of Sancho I, he had:
2 CONT # Andregoto Galíndez, who inherited the Aragonese county. She was queen of Pamplona by her marriage with her first cousin García Sanchez, king of Pamplona (925–970).[5]
2 CONT # Velasquita Galíndez,[3] first married Íñigo López de Estigi y Ciligueta.[6] She could also have been the wife of Count Fortún Jiménez of Aragon (fl. 943–958).[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo also sired several illegitimate sons: Guntislo, Sancho, Belasco, Banzo—father of a Galindo[8]—and Aznar.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
