2 CONC eached maturity[306], presumably aiming to exclude him from the succession in line with the practice in the Eastern Empire, where blindness was considered an impediment to ruling and therefore constituted an effective way of disem
2 CONC powering an opponent short of killing him (although many did succumb as a result of the treatment).  It is not recorded whether the punishment was carried out.  The same source records that Theodofredo settled in Córdoba.  The Chr
