2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the works of Washington Irving (pp 296-300)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Such was the state of Spain when, in the year of Redemption 701, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wamba_(king) Witiza] was elected to the Gothic  throne. The beginning of his reign gave promise of happy days to Spain. He redressed 
2 CONC grievances, moder.ucd the tributes of his subjects, and conducted himself with mingled mildness and energy in the administration of the laws. In a little while, however, he threw off the mask, and showed himself in his true nature
2 CONC , cruel and luxurious.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two of his relatives, sons of a preceding king, awakened his jealousy for the security of his throne. One of them, named Favila, duke of Cantabria, he put to death, and would have inflicted the same fate upon his son Pelayo, but t
2 CONC hat the youth was beyond his reach, being preserved by Providence for the future salvation of Spain. The other object of his suspicion was '''Theodofredo''', who lived retired from court. The violence of Witiza reached him e en in
2 CONC  his retirement. His eyes were put out, and he was immured within a castle at Cordova. Roderick, the youthful son of Theodofredo, escaped to Italy, where he received protection from the Romans.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chindasuinth was succeeded by his eldest son, Recceswinth, who continued his reforms. A younger son, '''Theodofred''', was blinded by Wamba. 
