1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CATALAN%20NOBILITY.htm#HugoIIAmpuriasB
2 CONT
2 CONT HUG [II] de Empúries, son of PONCE [I] Comte de Empúries & his wife Adelaida --- (-before 20 Jul 1128).  "…Ugo filio Pontio comiti Ympurias…" subscribed the charter dated 7 Sep 1071 which records an agreement between "Wuiellmum To
2 CONC losanum comitem" and "Raimundum comitem Barchinonensem et Carchanonensem et Raimundem filium eius" settling their dispute about "castello de Laurago" [Lauragais][1560].  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 20 Jul 1128 
2 CONC under which his son “Pontius Ugonis Emporitanensis comes” agreed peace with the church of Girona, naming “Ugo bonæ memoriæ pater meus…et Pontius avus meus”[1561].  He succeeded his father as Comte de Empúries.  “Ugo...comes” donat
2 CONC ed property to Santa Maria de Rodes by charter dated 25 Aug 1079[1562].  A charter dated 5 Oct 1091 records a dispute between the abbots of Sant Pere de Rodes and “sancti Stephani Balneolis cœnobii” in the court of “Ugo...comes...
2 CONC conjuge mea...Sancia”[1563].  "Ugo…comes Impuritanensis et Petralatensis necnon et Russilionensis" donated property to the abbey of Saint-Pierre de Rosas by charter dated 25 Mar 1116[1564]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SANCHA de Urgell, daughter of ARMENGOL [III] "él de Barbastro" Comte de Urgell & his [second wife [Clémence] de Bigorre].  A charter dated 5 Oct 1091 records a dispute between the abbots of Sant Pere de Rodes and “sancti S
2 CONC tephani Balneolis cœnobii” in the court of “Ugo...comes...conjuge mea...Sancia”[1565]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hug [II] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________ From Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh II, Count of Empúries
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh II (Catalan: Hug II) (c. 1035 – 1116) was the Count of Empúries from 1078 until his death. He was the eldest son of Ponç I and Adelaida de Besalú, and succeeded his father in Empúries while his brother, Berenguer, was given t
2 CONC he Viscounty of Peralada.
2 CONT
2 CONT In politics he was on good terms with the other Catalan princes. In 1085, he made an alliance of mutual self-defence with his neighbour, Giselbert II of Roussillon. In 1113–15, he and Ramon Berenguer III, Count of Barcelona, took 
2 CONC part in an expedition against the Balearics. He was described by the anonymous author of the Liber maiolichinus as Catalanicus heros (a Catalan hero).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh was involved in several disputes with the diocese of Girona, first with its canons and then with its bishop, Berenguer Guifré, over the tithes collected by the parish church of Santa Maria de Castelló. He made donations to th
2 CONC e monastery of Sant Pere de Rodes and made pilgrimages to Santiago de Compostela and the Holy Sepulchre at Jerusalem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh was married to Sancha, daughter of Ermengol IV of Urgell, which whom he had one child, the heir Ponç II.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Latin text of the Liber maiolichinus with Spanish introduction
