1 OCCU conde de Barcelona (1005-1035), Conde de Barcelona, Girona e Ausona, Count, Greve, Count of Barcelona, Comte, de Barcelone, de Girona, d'Ausona, Girona, and Ausona, and Ausona (1018-1035)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CATALAN%20NOBILITY.htm#BerenguerRamonIdied1035A Catalonia]
2 CONT * a) '''BERENGUER RAMON''' ([1000/05]-26 May 1035, bur Santa Maria de Ripoll). The Crónica de San Juan de la Peña names "Berenguer" as the son of "Remon Burrel conte de Barchinona"[261]. He succeeded his father in 1017 as BERENGUE
2 CONC R RAMON I "el Curvo" Comte de Barcelona, Girona, i Osona. — [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CATALAN%20NOBILITY.htm#BerenguerRamonIdied1035B '''See below''']....
2 CONT
