1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvira_Men%C3%A9ndez_de_Melanda
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00120382&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes de Melanda (c. 996 - 1022), foi condessa de Portugal e rainha consorte de Leão (1014-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Era natural da Galiza e filha de Tutadona Moniz e do conde Mendo Gonçalves, conde do primeiro condado de Portucale, co-regente de Leão durante a menoridade de Afonso V, seu genro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira casou-se em 1014 com Afonso V de Leão, donde nasceram:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Bermudo III de Leão (c. 1015-1037), rei de Leão;
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Sancha I de Leão (1013-1067), rainha titular de Leão e rainha consorte de Castela, casada em 1032 com Fernando I de Castela.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvira_Mendes
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes, sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia, (c. 996 – 20 December 1022), was Queen of León (1008-1022). Daughter of Count Mendo Gonçalves II of the First County of Portugal (House of Vímara P
2 CONC eres) and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was the mother of King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband, Alfonso V of León, Elvira had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Bermudo III of León (c.1015-1037)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Sancha of León (c.1020-1067), married Ferdinand I of León
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible, Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families Vol. 3 (chart 2186) by Michel L. Call ISBN 1-933194-22-7
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes, sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia, (c. 996 – 20 December 1022), was Queen of León (1008-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Count Mendo Gonçalves II of the First County of Portugal (House of Vímara Peres) and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was 
2 CONC the mother of King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband, Alfonso V of León, Elvira had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Bermudo III of León (c.1015-1037)
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Sancha of León (c.1020-1067), married Ferdinand I of Leon
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Elvira Mendes, sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia, (c. 996 – 20 December 1022), was Queen of León (1008-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Count Mendo Gonçalves II of the First County of Portugal (House of Vímara Peres) and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was 
2 CONC the mother of King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband, Alfonso V of León, Elvira had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bermudo III of León (c.1015-1037) 
2 CONT
