1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ermentrude de Roucy (d. 1005)
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of Renaud of Roucy and his wife, Alberade of Lorraine, daughter of Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermentrude married Alberic II of Mâcon and thus became a countess of Mâcon.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Ermentrude de Roucy (d. 1005)." Dictionary of Women Worldwide: 25,000 Women Through the Ages. . Retrieved June 01, 2018 from Encyclopedia.com: http://www.encyclopedia.com/women/dictionaries-thesauruses-pictures-and-press-rel
2 CONC eases/ermentrude-de-roucy-d-1005
2 CONT
2 CONT Countess of Burgundy. Name variations: Ermentrude de Rouci; Ermentrude Rheims; Irmtrude. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died Mar 5, 1005; dau. of Renaud or Rainald de Roucy and Alberade of Lorraine (930–973); 
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Othon-Guillaume also known as Otto William, count of Burgundy, c. 982 (died 1026); 
2 CONT
2 CONT children: 
2 CONT *Agnes of Aquitaine (c. 995–1068);
2 CONT * Gerberga of Burgundy (who m. William II, count of Provence); 
2 CONT *Matilda of Burgundy (who m. Landeric, count of Nevers); 
2 CONT *Renaud I (990–1057), 1st count of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermentrude de Roucy (d. 1005) - Dictionary definition of Ermentrude de Roucy (d. 1005) | Encyclopedia.com: FREE online dictionary 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ermentrude_de_Roucy
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00020659&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Alt death year: 3/5/1005
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermentrude, daughter of Count Renaud of Rheims married Otto-William, Count of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had two sons and three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Guy had been associated as count of Mâcon from 995, he died young in 1006
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Matilda, married Landri of Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Geberga, married Guilhem II of Provence
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Renaud I, Count of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Agnes, married firstly William V of Aquitaine, secondly Geoffrey II of Anjou
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto married the four-times widowed Adelaide of Anjou late in life and they had no known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Othon-Guillaume de BOURGOGNE and Ermentrude de REIMS et COUCY
