1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/cfragobs.htm#HuguesPercheGatinaisMBeatrixMacon
2 CONT * https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/cfragobs.htm#GeoffroyGatinaisdied991
2 CONT * The Henry Project: The Ancestors of King Henry II of England: [https://fasg.org/projects/henryproject/data/beatr000.htm Béatrix de Mâcon].
2 CONT - https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9atrice_de_M%C3%A2con,_fille_d%27Aubry_II_de_M%C3%A2con
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Beatrice de Mâcon1 b. 974
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Albéric II de Mâcon b. before 931, d. between 981 and 982 Mother	Ermentrude de Roucy b. 958, d. 5 March 1005 Charts	Descendants of Charlemage
2 CONT      Beatrice de Mâcon was born in 974. She was the daughter of Albéric II de Mâcon and Ermentrude de Roucy. Beatrice de Mâcon married Geoffroy I, comte de Gâtinais, son of Geoffrey de Vexin, before 1000. Family Geoffroy I, comte 
2 CONC de Gâtinais b. 970 Child	 Geoffroy II "Ferreol", comte de Gâtinais+ b. c 1004, d. 1046 Citations [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 92-32.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice de Macon 1 Born: ABT 975 in Macon, Saone-et-Loire, Bourgogne, France Father: Alberic II Count of Macon, & Salins b: ABT 949 in Macon, Saone-et-Loire, Bourgogne, France  Mother: Ermentrude (Irmgard) de Roucy b: ABT 953 in 
2 CONC Reims, Marne, Champagne, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Geoffroy I "Ferreol" Count of Gatinais b: ABT 970 in Gatinais, Loiret, Orleanais/Centre, France Married: BEF 999 Children: Geoffroy II "Ferreol" Count of Gatinais b: ABT 1000 in Chateau Landon, Seine-et-Marne, Ile-de-Fr
2 CONC ance, France Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists, 7th Edition, by Frederick Lewis Weis, additions by Walter Lee Sheppard Jr., 1999 Page: 118-22
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------
2 CONT Beatrice de Macon was born 974 to Aubry II de Macon (935-982) and Ermentrude de Roucy (-c1004) and died 1030 of unspecified causes. She married Geoffroy Ier du Gatinais (?-?) 974 . She married Hugues du Perche (-c1000) . Notable a
2 CONC ncestors include Charlemagne (747-814). Ancestors are from France, Belgium, Germany. Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Offspring of Beatrice de Macon and Geoffroy Ier du Gatinais (?-?) 
2 CONT Joined with Aubry du Gatinais (c985-c1030) 	984 	1029 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Offspring of Beatrice de Macon and Hugues du Perche (-c1000) 
2 CONT Joined with Geoffrey, Count of Gâtinais (?-c1044) 999 Gastinais, France 	
2 CONT 26 December 1045 	Ermengarde of Anjou (c1018-1076)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lietaud de Yevres (c995-aft1050) 	994 	1049 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://familypedia.wikia.com/wiki/Beatrice_de_Macon_%28974-1030%29#Children
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT As an aside, this resolution of the chronological difficulties with identifying Ermentrude as wife both of Aubri and Otto-William requires the supposition that Aubri married twice, and that Beatrice, wife of Geoffrey of Gatinais, 
2 CONC ancestress of the Anjou Counts, must have been by the earlier wife. The author hypothesizes that she may have been a sister of Hugh Capet. While not explained, the reasoning would seem to be based on the name Beatrice, a name foun
2 CONC d in that family since Robert (I) married Beatrice of Vermandois. Other writings in the same compilation add a generation, making Beatrice daughter of Aubri by a daughter of Geoffrey, Vicomte of Orleans, who in turn is made brothe
2 CONC r-in-law, of Hugh Capet.)
2 CONT
2 CONT taf
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources and notes
2 CONT ‡ General 	
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aubry_II_de_M%C3%A2con 
