2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkcounty.htm#GaucherIISalinsMbefore1044AremburgeB
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GAUCHER [II] de Salins''', son of HUMBERT [II] Seigneur des Salins & his wife Ermenburge --- (-13 Apr ---).  "Vualcherius miles de Salinis" confirmed donations of "Humberto patri suo" by undated charter, dated to after 1039, in
2 CONC  the presence of "Hugo archiepiscopus, frater Vualcherii…"[1118].   Seigneur de Salins.  “Galcherius Salinensis dominus” swore allegiance to the abbot of Agaune for “Bracon cum appendiciis suis...et in Cicon illud quod dicitur cas
2 CONC trum sancti Mauritii...”, naming “Guidone archidiacono nepote meo”, by undated charter[1119].  The necrology of Besançon cathedral records the death in Apr “E” of “Valcherius fr.  H. Archiep.”[1120]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 1044) as her second husband, AREMBURGE, widow of ---, daughter of ---.  "Aremburgis uxor Vualcherii de Salins" made a donation to Cluny dated [1087], signed by "Vuilelmi filii sui, Arberti filius eius"[1121], provi
2 CONC ding the only indication that she must have been married before marrying Gaucher, as well as "Vualterii filii eius" the latter presumably referring to her son by Gaucher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gaucher [II] & his wife had one child: 
