1 NOTE He ruled from 642.
1 NOTE King of Visigothic Hispania. His kingship was the result of a usurping the throne from Tulga, (Tulca) in a coup. Despite his great age, he was already 79 years old when he laid seige upon a place and won; he was a vereran at that 
2 CONC age of 79 of the Leowigild campaigns and various religious rebellions after conversions from Arianism were forced.
2 CONT Visigoth Kings who ruled before Chindasuinth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tulga King of the Visigoths. Ruled began about 640.
2 CONT Chintila King of Visgoths ruled 636/639 through 640.
2 CONT Sisenand King of the Visigoths ruled 631 through 636.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT 1: Collins, Roger. Visigothic Spain, 409-711.
2 CONT Blackwell publishing 2004.
2 CONT 2: King, P.D., King Chindasuinth and the first territorial law code of the Visigothic kingdon.
2 CONT Edward James-Oxford-Clarendon Press 1980, PP. 131-157.
1 NOTE Chindasvinto (também chamado Chindasvindo ou Quindasvinto) (c. 562 — 653) foi rei visigodo da Hispânia, um dos mais notáveis da sua estirpe e cujo nome em godo era provavelmente Kindswinth ou Chindaswinth. Foi escolhido para ocupa
2 CONC r o trono no ano de 642, quando já era idoso, tendo-se dedicado a pacificar o reino, dominar as facções dissidentes e a submeter a inquieta nobreza. Ganhou a merecida fama de sábio legislador pelas suas importantes realizações. Co
2 CONC nvocou o VII Concílio de Toledo (16-10-646), associou o seu filho Recesvindo ao trono (649), consolidou a inconstante monarquia visigoda e protegeu as artes e as letras do seu reino.
