2 CONT Viscount of Milhaud 
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9renger_de_Millau
2 CONT
2 CONT Berenger Ist Millau then Berenger Carlat , born about 1025 , died about 1080 was Viscount of Millau and Rodez in 1051, and, by marriage, Viscount of Carlat . He was the son of Richard II, Viscount of Millau and Rodez, and Rixinde 
2 CONC de Narbonne .
2 CONT
2 CONT «b»Biography «/b»
2 CONT Around 1080, with his wife Adèle and Nobilia de Lodeve, mother of Adèle, and their three children Richard, Gilbert and Raymond, he made a donation to the abbey founded by Gausbert, a monk in Saint-Amans de Rodez, with a land betwe
2 CONC en four crosses forming a dependent safeguard of the castle of Mandulphe, and for the spiritual of the parish of Junhac. The name of Montsalvy ( Montis Salvii ) will only appear in 1093 in a Celestine III bull that directly links 
2 CONC the new abbey to the Holy See.
2 CONT
2 CONT «b»Family «/b»
2 CONT Before 1050, he married Adèle, viscountess of Carlat, daughter of Girbert, viscount of Carlat, and Nobilia, viscountess of Lodève. They had at least three sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) Richard III Millau († 1135), father of Hugues I st, († 1159), Viscount of Carlat, Count of Rodez
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.) Gilbert of Millau († 1111)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.) Raymond
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LRHD-9QV
