1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From fmgMedlands  [1645] Marca Hispanica (1688), Appendix, CCCC, col. 1289
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         GUILLEM Dalmau (-after 11 Jun 1142).  Udalgar Bishop of Elna and “Gaufredum vicecomitem de Rocabertíno” reached agreement by charter dated 11 Jun 1142, subscribed by “Gaufredi vicecomitis de Rocabertíno...Guillermi Dalm
2 CONC atii fratris eius...”[1645]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Curator Note: a cross check with the Wikipedia page for the Roman Catholic Diocese of Perpignan-Elne does not identify a person Guillem Dalmau as a bishop during this time frame in its list of bishops.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noting in the genealogical tree of Rocaberti in the The Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana it shows two brothers named Dalmau.  I believe that to be an error and the name of the canon of Elna actually Guillem Dalmau as indicated in fmgMed
2 CONC lands, however it’s also important to note the differences in the death date with fmgMedlands giving it as after 11 June 1142  and the GEC as 1072.  The GEC also shows an identical entry fro Dalmau canon of Girona dead in 1072.  T
2 CONC he Roman Catholic Diocese of Perpignan–Elne Is located in Elna, The Roman Catholic Diocese of Perpignan–Elne adjacent to the northern Spanish frontier, ie Catalonia. A cross check with the list of bishops serving the diocese of Ge
2 CONC rona show no bishops with this name.
2 CONT
2 CONT The proper generation for this person is in question.
