2 CONT
2 CONT GEOFFROY [II] de Gâtinais, son of HUGUES du Perche Comte de Gâtinais & his wife Beatrix de Mâcon (-30 Apr [1043/45]).  
2 CONT *His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 26 May 1028 under which Francon Bishop of Paris agreed with "Albericum illius supradicti Gosfredi filium et heredum", concerning a prior grant by the bishop's predecessor to "Gosfri
2 CONC do comiti Landonensi castri", with the approval of "fratribus ipsius Alberici, filiis Hugonis Pertice…Gosfredo et Letoldo"[204].  A genealogy presented by Foulques IV "le Réchin" Comte d'Anjou to the bishop of Angers in [1085], ju
2 CONC stifying the annulment of his fourth marriage with the daughter of Gauthier Comte de Brienne, lists "ex Letaldo, Albericus natus est, ex Alberico, Beatrix, ex Beatrice, Gosfredus de Castello Landonensi, ex Gaufrido, Gaufridus et F
2 CONC ulco presens"[205].  
2 CONT *He succeeded his half-brother as Comte de Gâtinais, Seigneur de Château-Landon.  
2 CONT *The fact that Aubry Comte de Gâtinais and Geoffroy [II] Comte de Gâtinais were two different individuals, the inevitable conclusion from the two sources cited, is somewhat clouded by the Historia Comitum Andegavorum which records
2 CONC  that "Gaufridus Martellus…nepotibus suis" were "filiis Adhelæ sororis suæ et Alberici comitis de Gastinais"[206], and by the Chronicle of Saint-Maxence which names "Alberici Contracti comitis de Gastina" as father of "Goffredus e
2 CONC t Fulco Rechin"[207]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1035]) as her first husband, ERMENGARDE d'Anjou, daughter of FOULQUES III "Nerra" Comte d'Anjou & his second wife Hildegard [de Metz] ([1018]-murdered church of Fleury-sur-Ouche, Côte d’Or 18 Mar 1076, bur Abbaye de Saint-Sein
2 CONC e, Côte d'Or).  
2 CONT *The Historiæ Andegavensis names "Goffridi de Castro Landono et Ermengardis filia Fulconis Comitis Andegavensis" as parents of "Fulco comes Andegavensis"[208].  Her second marriage is deduced from a genealogy of the Comtes d'Anjou
2 CONC  which names "Fulco (pater) Gosfridus et Ermengardis (mater) Gosfridus (et) Fulco (et) Hildegardis, de altero patre, filia Roberti ducis fratris Henrici regis"[209].  
2 CONT *She married secondly ([1048]) Robert I "le Vieux" Duke of Burgundy.  
2 CONT *The necrology of Molesme records the death "XV Kal Apr" of "Robertus dux Burgundie et Ermengardis uxor eius"[210].  She was murdered with her second husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Geoffroy & his wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. HILDEGARDE de Château-Landon (-after 1060).  
2 CONT *The Historia of Monk Aimon records the marriage of "Joscelinum de Cortinaco" and "filiam comitis Gaufridi Foerole" by whom he had one daughter[211].  She is named in Burke´s Peerage but the primary source on which this is based h
2 CONC as not yet been identified[212].   
2 CONT *m ([1060]) as his first wife, JOSCELIN [I] Seigneur de Courtenay, son of ATHON Châtelain de Châteaurenard & his wife --- ([1034]-after 1065). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. GEOFFROY de Château-Landon ([1040]-[1096/97]).  
2 CONT *The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum records that "Gosfridus Martellus filius Fulconis", being childless, appointed "nepotibus suis Gosfrido Barbato et Fulconi Rechin" as his heirs[213].  The Historia Comitum Andegavorum records that "
2 CONC Gaufridus Martellus…nepotibus suis" were "filiis Adhelæ sororis suæ et Alberici comitis de Gastinais"[214].  "Gaufredus comitatus Andecavensis naturalis heres" made donations to Marmoutier dated 1055 in which he names "nepotibus m
2 CONC eis…Fulcone vincocinensium comite naturali, Gaufredo et altero Fulcone"[215].  
2 CONT *He succeeded in 1060 as GEOFFROY III "le Barbu" Comte d'Anjou.  "Goffridi comitis et Agnetis comitissæ…" witnessed the charter dated 26 Feb 1062, recorded in the dating clause as "anno principatus Gaufredi comitis tertii IIo", wh
2 CONC ich records an agreement of confraternity between Saint-Maurice d´Angers and La Trinité de Vendôme[216].  "Goffridus comes" restored property donated by "avia mea bone memorie Hildegardis comitissa…filie sue matri mee…Ermengardi…A
2 CONC delait Teotisca que fuerat postrema avunculi mei uxor…avunculi mei Goffredi comitis" to the monastery of La Charité Sainte-Marie d´Anjou by undated charter[217].  
2 CONT *The Chronicon Turonensi records that "Gaufridus Barbatus…Comes" destroyed "Turoniæ, Abbatiam Majoris-Monasterii", after which he was captured by his brother Foulques and held captive for thirty years "apud Chainonem"[218].  Willi
2 CONC am of Malmesbury and Orderic Vitalis both record that he was deposed in 1068 and imprisoned by his brother at the castle of Chinon for more than thirty years[219].  The Chronicon Vindocinense records that "Fulconi fratri Gaufridi 
2 CONC comitis Andegavorum" captured "Salmuri castri…Kal Mar" in 1067 and "II Kal Apr" captured and imprisoned "fratrem suum…comes Gaufredus junior…Barbatum" until his death, although another paragraph of the Chronicon dates the capture 
2 CONC to 1068[220].  The Chronica Rainaldi records that "Goffridus junior…Barbatum" was betrayed by "Fulconi fratri suo…Non Apr" in 1067 and captured in 1068[221].  
2 CONT *m (before 1060) JULIENNE de Langeais, daughter of HAMELIN [II] Seigneur de Langeais & [his wife Helvise de Mondoubleau] (-after 7 Aug 1067).  "Geoffroi le Barbu…[et] Julienne son épouse" confirmed the donation by "Bouchard le Bre
2 CONC ton" to Saint-Nicolas d´Angers, by charter dated to after 14 Nov 1060[222].  Her parentage is confirmed by a charter dated to [1068/82] under which "Hugues de Langeais", with the consent of "ses frères Hamelin et Geoffroi le doyen
2 CONC …son suzerain Geoffroi de Mayenne", donated property to Bourgeuil, subscribed by "comtesse Hameline", as well as a line of commentary in the cartulary of Bourgeuil which states that the subscriber was "filia Hamelini de Langiaco, 
2 CONC uxor Goffridi Barbati comitis Andegav"[223].  "Geoffroi le Barbu…Juliette femme de Geoffroi et Foulque frère de Geoffroi" subscribed the charter dated 7 Aug 1067 which records the donation by "Robert de Sablé et sa femme Avoie" to
2 CONC  Marmoutier[224].  
2 CONT *[m AGNES, daughter of --- (-after 26 Feb 1062).  "Goffridi comitis et Agnetis comitissæ…" witnessed the charter dated 26 Feb 1062, recorded in the dating clause as "anno principatus Gaufredi comitis tertii IIo", which records an 
2 CONC agreement of confraternity between Saint-Maurice d´Angers and La Trinité de Vendôme[225].  The dating clause indicates that this document is correctly dated to 1062, and suggests that the witness was Geoffroy III Comte d´Anjou and
2 CONC  therefore that "Agnetis comitissæ" was his wife.  This conclusion causes a considerable difficulty as Geoffroy's wife Julienne is named in charters dated 1060 and 1067.  Another possibility is that "Agnetis comitissæ" was the fir
2 CONC st wife of Geoffroy´s predecessor, Geoffroy II "Martel" Comte d´Anjou, although if this is correct it is suprising that she signed in place of Geoffroy III´s wife.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. FOULQUES de Château-Landon (1043-14 Apr 1109, bur Anjou Sainte-Trinité).  
2 CONT *The Historiæ Andegavensis names "Goffridi de Castro Landono et Ermengardis filia Fulconis Comitis Andegavensis" as parents of "Fulco comes Andegavensis"[226].  "Gaufredus comitatus Andecavensis naturalis heres" made donations to 
2 CONC Marmoutier dated 1055 in which he names "nepotibus meis…Fulcone vincocinensium comite naturali, Gaufredo et altero Fulcone"[227].  
2 CONT *He succeeded, after deposing his brother, as FOULQUES IV "le Rechin" Comte d'Anjou.  The Chronicon Vindocinense records that "Fulconi fratri Gaufridi comitis Andegavorum" captured "Salmuri castri…Kal Mar" in 1067 and "II Kal Apr"
2 CONC  captured and imprisoned "fratrem suum…comes Gaufredus junior…Barbatum" until his death, although another paragraph of the Chronicon dates the capture to 1068[228].  
2 CONT *He ceded Château-Landon and Gâtinais to Philippe I King of France in 1069 in return for the king's recognition of his accession as count[229].  
2 CONT *He expelled the Normans from Maine but peace was imposed by William I King of England[230].  
2 CONT *The necrology of Angers Cathedral records the death "XVIII Kal Mai" of "Fulco…comes Andagavensis nepos Gaufridi prioris Martelli"[231].  The necrology of Vendôme La Trinité records the death "XVIII Kal Mai" of "Fulco comes Andega
2 CONC vorum"[232].  A list of anniversaries of Vendôme La Trinité records the death "XVIII Kal Mai" of "Fulconis comitis qui iacet in Aquaria"[233].  The Chronicon Vindocinense records the death "XVIII Kal Mai" in 1109 of "Fulco comes A
2 CONC ndegavorum…frater comitis Gosfridi…Barbatus" and his burial "in monasterio nostro Andegavense S. Trinitatis"[234].  
2 CONT *m firstly ([1068]) HILDEGARDE de Baugency, daughter of LANCELIN [II] de Baugency & his wife --- (-before 1070).  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum refers to the first wife of "Fulco Rechin" as "filiam Lancelini de Baugenciaco"[235].
2 CONC   The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT *m secondly (1070, divorced) as her first husband, ERMENGARDE de Bourbon, daughter of ARCHAMBAUD [IV] "le Fort" Sire de Bourbon & his wife Béliarde ---.  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum names "Ermengardim filiam Archenbaldi Fortis 
2 CONC de Borbone" as second wife of "Fulco Rechin", recording that he divorced her[236].  She married secondly Guillaume Seigneur de Jaligny.  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum names her second husband "Guillelmo Jalinniaci ortam" when rec
2 CONC ording the marriage of her daughter by this second marriage[237].  
2 CONT *m thirdly (21 Jan 1076, divorced 1080) ORENGARDE de Châtelaillon, daughter of ISEMBART Seigneur de Châtelaillon & his wife ---.  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the dating clause of a charter dated 21 Jan "1070" (reda
2 CONC ted to 1076) which records this as the date of the marriage of "comes Fulco" and "Aurengarde, filia Isemberti de Castello Allione"[238].  Comte Foulque "Rechin" donated property to Saint-Nicolas d´Angers, for the salvation of "sa 
2 CONC femme Orengarde", by charter dated 17 May 1076[239].  She became a nun after her divorce.  
2 CONT *m fourthly (after 1080, divorced before 1089) --- de Brienne, daughter of GAUTHIER I Comte de Brienne & his wife Eustachie Ctss de Bar-sur-Saône .  A genealogy presented by Foulques IV "le Réchin" Comte d'Anjou to the bishop of A
2 CONC ngers in [1085], justifying the annulment of his fourth marriage with the daughter of Gauthier Comte de Brienne, lists "ex Letaldo, Albericus natus est, ex Alberico, Beatrix, ex Beatrice, Gosfredus de Castello Landonensi, ex Gaufr
2 CONC ido, Gaufridus et Fulco presens"[240].  
2 CONT *m fifthly (1089, divorced [15 May 1092]) as her first husband, BERTRADE de Montfort, daughter of SIMON I Comte de Montfort-l'Amaury & his third wife Agnès d'Evreux (-Fontevrault end-1115/1116, bur church of the priory of Hautes-B
2 CONC ruyères, Saint-Remy-l’Honoré, Yvelines).  Her parentage is recorded by Orderic Vitalis[241].  The Gesta Consulum Andegavorum refers to the "third wife" of "Fulco Rechin" as "sororem Amalrici de Monte Forti"[242].  She married seco
2 CONC ndly (15 May 1092, repudiated 1104) as his second wife, Philippe I King of France (-29 Aug 1108), who abducted Bertrade from her first husband and married her bigamously[243].  The De Genere Comitum Flandrensium, Notæ Parisienses 
2 CONC names "Fulconi Richin Andegavensi comiti uxorem suam nomine Bertradam" as second wife of King Philippe whom he abducted from her first husband after repudiating his first wife[244].  William of Tyre records this marriage[245].  Po
2 CONC pe Urban II at the Council of Autun excommunicated the king 16 Oct 1094, confirmed at the Council of Clermont 18/28 Nov 1095[246].  The church finally admitted the validity of the marriage after the Council of Paris 2 Dec 1104[247
2 CONC ].  Orderic Vitalis alleges that Bertrade tried to poison her stepson Louis so her own sons could succeed to the throne[248].  "Fulco iunior Andegavensium comes Fulconis comitis filius" donated property to the abbey of Fontevraud 
2 CONC with the consent of "Bertrade regina matre meo, Philipo fratre meo" by charter dated to [1109/1112/13][249].  
2 CONT *Comte Foulques IV & his first wife had one child: Ermengarde d'Anjou (1068-1146)
2 CONT *Comte Foulques IV & his second wife had one child: Geoffroy d'Anjou (1073-1106)
2 CONT *Comte Foulques IV & his fifth wife had one child: Foulques d'Anjou (1092-1144)
2 CONT
