2 CONT
2 CONT '''Engelbert III de Brienne ''' (né vers 960 - † après 1008), est comte de Brienne à la fin du Xe siècle et au début du XIe siècle. Il est le fils d'[https://www.geni.com/people/Engelbert-II-comte-de-Brienne/6000000003051212348 En
2 CONC gelbert II de Brienne], deuxième comte de Brienne connu''[1]'' /!\ . .. ... 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ''[1]''-https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/chambrien.htm#EngelbertIIIBriennedied1008B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ENGELBERT''' [II] ['''de Brienne'''], son of --- .  His existence is confirmed by the charter dated to [1027] under which "Ingelbertus…comes" donated property to Montiérender naming "quondam Ingelbertus comes predecessor noster
2 CONC "[7].  The dating suggests that the earlier Engelbert must have been a different person from Engelbert [I] (see above).  This source does not specify that Engelbert's predecessor was his father.  Comte de Brienne.  1004/08. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly WANDALMODIS, daughter of --- Comte & his wife Adela de Salins.  A manuscript genealogy, dated to the early 12th century, records "Letaldus comes Vesoncius et Umbertus comes Marisconensis fratres", adding "ex Umbert
2 CONC o, Adala comitissa, ex Adala Windesmodis soror matris vestræ non german, ex Windesmode Ingelbertus et Witdo de Upione"[8]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly as her second husband, ALIX de Sens, widow of GEOFFROY de Joigny, daughter of RENARD [I] Comte de Sens & his wife ---.  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the wife of "comes de Brena super Albam
2 CONC  Engelbertus" as "comitissam Ioviniaci viduam de primo marito"[9].  She died before her husband, as the same passage refers to her son-in-law inheriting Joigny after her death and subsequently building the first castle of Joinvill
2 CONC e with the help of his father-in-law.  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified. 
