1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ENGELBERT [III] de Brienne, son of ENGELBERT [II] de Brienne & his first wife Wandelmodis --- (-1035 or after).  A manuscript genealogy, dated to the early 12th century, records "Letaldus comes Vesoncius et Umbertu
2 CONC s comes Marisconensis fratres", adding "ex Umberto, Adala comitissa, ex Adala Windesmodis soror matris vestræ non german, ex Windesmode Ingelbertus et Witdo de Upione"[18].  "Ingelbertus…comes" donated property to Montiérender by 
2 CONC charter dated [1027] "actum Breona castello" in which he names "quondam Ingelbertus comes predecessor noster", subscribed by "Adeledis comitisse, Wuarneri, Gocelmi, Guntardi, Bernard"[19], although "Adeledis comitisse" has not bee
2 CONC n identified.  It is possible that she was an earlier wife of Comte Engelbert [III].  This source does not specify that Engelbert's predecessor was his father, but the primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been i
2 CONC dentified.  Comte de Brienne.  1035. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m PETRONILLE, daughter of --- (-after 6 Jun 1050).  "Comes Breonensium Gualterus cum matre sua Petronilla" donated property to Montiérender by charter dated 28 Dec 1035[20], presumably following the death of their father/husband a
2 CONC lthough this is not stated in the document.  "Comite Waltero et matre eius Petronilla" are named as present in a charter dated [12 Jun 1050 or before] under which "Bosoni iuvenis" donated property to Montiérender, naming "pater ei
2 CONC us Elbertus"[21].  "Walterus comes Brenensis…mater mea Petronilla" donated property to Montiérender by charter dated 6 Jun 1050, subscribed by "Letaldi comitis Cereaci"[22]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Engelbert [III] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.         GAUTHIER [I] de Brienne (-[1090]) x EUSTACHIE de Tonnerre, daughter of MILO [V] Comte de Tonnerre et de Bar-sur-Seine & his wife Aceka ---.  1072/[1100/05].  Ctss de Bar-sur-Seine. Comte Gauthier [I] & his wife had fiv
2 CONC e children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         ENGELBERT de Brienne (-after 1082).
2 CONT >b)         ERARD [I] de Brienne (-[1114/25], bur Montier-en-Der)
2 CONT >c)         MILON de Brienne (-[1126]).
2 CONT >d)         daughter
2 CONT >e)         MANTIA de Brienne
