2 CONT 1.         GAUCHER [III] de Salins (-after 1087).  "Dominus Vualcherius, Salinensis oppidi prefectus, filius alterius" donated property to Romainmotier by undated charter, dated to before 1057[1122].   "Vualcherius filius Vualcher
2 CONC ii filii Humberti" donated property to Romainmotier, with the consent of "uxori meæ Beatrici…et filius meus Humbertus, tunc parvulus", by charter dated 1084[1123].   “Guichardus eiusdem ecclesiæ canonicus et archidiaconus” donated
2 CONC  property inherited from “matris meæ Ermenburgæ...avus meus genitor eius Humbertus...Salinis”, and which “frater meus Humbertus” later granted him, to Besançon Saint-Etienne by charter dated 27 Dec 1087, the same charter recording
2 CONC  that later “Gualcherius avunculi eius Gualcherii filius”, anticipating his inheritance from the donor, claimed the property from the church but that “Gualcherius et filii mei Humbertus et Hugo” confirmed the donation[1124].  An u
2 CONC ndated charter records the donation to Balerne abbey made by “senem Waucherium” and later confirmed by “Humberto et...a genere suo...usque ad dominam Nicolam cujus sponsus...Simon de Comarceio...eiusque heredes Hugo, Waucherius”[1
2 CONC 125].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' BEATRIX, daughter of ---.  "Vualcherius filius Vualcherii filii Humberti" donated property to Romainmotier, with the consent of "uxori meæ Beatrici…et filius meus Humbertus, tunc parvulus", by charter dated 1084[1126].   
2 CONT
