2 CONT Ermesinde, regente de Barcelona1,2 b. circa 972, d. 1 March 1057
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Roger I "el Viejo", comte de Comminges3 b. circa 945, d. after April 1011 Mother	Adelais de Pons3 b. circa 945, d. after April 1011
2 CONT      Ermesinde, regente de Barcelona was the daughter of Roger I, comte de Carcassone, and Adelais, sister of Baldwin de Pons.4 Also called Ermesende de Foix.5 She was born circa 972. She was the daughter of Roger I "el Viejo", co
2 CONC mte de Comminges and Adelais de Pons.3 Ermesinde, regente de Barcelona married Ramón Borrell, conde de Barcelona, son of Borrell II, conde de Barcelona, Gerona y Ausona and Luitgarde de Toulouse, between 990 and 991.1,4 Ermesinde,
2 CONC  regente de Barcelona was a witness where Berenguer Ramón I "el Curvo", conde de Barcelona, Gerona y Ausona entirely under the control of his mother -- but made some settlement of the political conditions of the country, by recogn
2 CONC izing, granting or codifying the fueros and liberties of Barcelona, which at that time included Gerona, Ausona and Manresa between 1018 and 1035.6 Ermesinde, regente de Barcelona entirely controlled the county of Barcelona, then r
2 CONC uled by her son Berenguer-Ramon I, between 1018 and 1035. She established herself in Gerona and claimed the greater part of her grandson, Ramon Berenguer I's, dominions as her own circa 1036.6 She was a witness where Ramón Berengu
2 CONC er I "el Viejo", conde de Barcelona able to extend his influence in two directions after a preliminary struggle with his grandmother, who had established herself in Gerona and claimed the greater part of his dominions as her own, 
2 CONC and extended his frontiers as far as Barbastro by conquests from the Moors; and in other directions, more especially in the south, where Moorish chieftains and governors paid him tribute and acknowledged his supremacy.6 Ermesinde,
2 CONC  regente de Barcelona died on 1 March 1057.1,4 Ermesinde, regente de Barcelona was buried in the Cathedral, Girona, Catalonia, Spain. Family Ramón Borrell, conde de Barcelona b. 972, d. 1018 Children	 Berenguer Ramón I "el Curvo",
2 CONC  conde de Barcelona, Gerona y Ausona+ b. 1000, d. 6 Apr 10355 Adelaide de Barcelona+ b. 1004, d. 10512 Citations [S204] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 291-34. [S1316] Reyes y Reinos Genealogias, online www.homar.org, España - 09.F. [S20
2 CONC 4] Roderick W. Stuart, RfC, 291-35. [S438] Theroff's Royal Genealogies, online http://pages.prodigy.net/ptheroff/, Foix.txt. [S935] LUIS K. W. (e-mail address), Re: Sibil de Barcelona? In "Re: Sibil de Barcelona?," newsgroup messa
2 CONC ge 2001-05-27 07:53:50 PST. [S512] H. J. Chaytor, Chaytor, H. J., chap. 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ermesenda de Carcasona (972-1058) o Ermesinda, fue una de las mujeres que ostentaron mayor poder real en toda la Edad Media europea, y seguramente también llegaríamos al Renacimiento y lo sobrepasaríamos. Una mujer enérgica, que n
2 CONC o duda en acompañar a su marido en el campo de batalla montada a caballo, desafiando las convenciones. Un ser extraordinario en un mundo de hombres, y hombres muy brutos, pues en aquel tiempo lo que sabían hacer mejor en el Condad
2 CONC o de Barcelona era la guerra. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dudo mucho que hoy existan mujeres que gobiernen tanto y durante tanto tiempo como lo hizo ella. No se me ocurre ningún ejemplo, a excepción de Isabel la Católica, aunque ella gobernó junto a su esposo y, si la memoria no me falla
2 CONC , no excomulgó a ninguno de sus nietos.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ermesinde_of_Carcassonne
