1 OCCU Countess of Barcelona
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Estefania_Ramon
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ - https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Estefania_de_Barcelone ''(draft)''
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide (1004-1051), che sposò, in prime nozze (circa 1018), Ruggero di Tosny[23] (circa 990- 1040, morì combattendo i Mori della penisola iberica) e poi si risposò con Riccardo d'Evreux[24]. https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raimond
2 CONC o_Borrell_di_Barcellona
2 CONT
2 CONT ''{merged clones with this marriage, but in the history of https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-I-count-of-Evreux/6000000005622785343?through=6000000003210324146, she is not mentioned. ..& the source cited on the wiki FR is notorio
2 CONC usly untrustworthy. (Cutted) }
2 CONT --------
2 CONT ADELAIDA [Papia] de Barcelona, daughter of RAMÓN BORELL I Conde de Barcelona & his wife Ermesinde de Carcassonne.  
2 CONT
2 CONT married Roger I de Tosny "d'Espagne" de Conches
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Helbert Helinant Vuasco Adelisa m. Guillaume FitzOsbern Seigneur de Breteuil
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN NOBILITY.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Adémar de Chabannes records that "Normanni duce Rotgerio", who had been fighting Saracens in Spain, asked "comitissa Barzelonensi Ermensende…vidua" for the hand of her daughter, but does not name the latter[1820].
2 CONC   It is not clear that "dux Rotgerius" is Roger de Conches, particularly as it seems surprising that Adémar would have accorded him the title "dux".  It is assumed that this marriage proposal took place in 1018 or soon after: if i
2 CONC t had taken place much later, there would have been little reason to have referred to the bride's mother as "vidua".  In addition, the other events recorded by Adémar in the same paragraph, all relate to 1016/18.  The Chronici Hug
2 CONC onis Floriacensis records that "Rotgerius filius Rodulfi comitis" married "sororem Raymundi-Berengarii Stephaniam" in Spain, specifying that she later married "rex Hispaniæ Garsias"[1821], but this account is even more confused an
2 CONC d clearly conflates several different individuals.  The Chronico S Petri Vivi Senonensi records the same marriage using the same wording[1822].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger [I] & his [first/second] wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         HELBERT (-killed in battle [1040]).  Guillaume de Jumièges names "Helbert et Hélinant" as the two sons of "Roger du Ternois" when recording that they were killed with their father by "Roger de Beaumont" during their reb
2 CONC ellion against Guillaume II Duke of Normandy in the early years of the duke's reign[1825]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         HELINANT (-killed in battle [1040]).  Guillaume de Jumièges names "Helbert et Hélinant" as the two sons of "Roger du Ternois" when recording that they were killed with their father by "Roger de Beaumont" during their re
2 CONC bellion against Guillaume II Duke of Normandy in the early years of the duke's reign[1826]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         VUASCO .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   1037/1045. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         ADELISA (-6 Oct <nowiki>----</nowiki>, bur Abbaye de Lire).  Guillaume de Jumièges names "Adelise fille de Roger du Ternois" as wife of "Guillaume fils d'Osbern, proche parent du duc Guillaume", recording that her husba
2 CONC nd buried her in the monastery of Lire which he had built[1827].  Robert of Torigny's De Immutatione Ordinis Monachorum records that "Willermus filius Osberni Normanniæ dapifer et cognatus Willermi ducis…Aelizam uxorem suam filiam
2 CONC  Rogeri de Toeneio" was buried in the monastery of Lire[1828].  The necrology of Lyre monastery records the death "6 Oct" of "Adeliz uxor Willelmi hujus loci fundatoris"[1829].  The necrology of the monastery of Ouche records the 
2 CONC death "6 Oct" of "mater Willelmi Britolii Adeliza"[1830].  m as his first wife, GUILLAUME FitzOsbern Seigneur de Breteuil, son of OSBERN de Crépon & his wife Emma d'Ivry (-killed in battle Cassel, Flanders 22 Feb 1071, bur Abbaye 
2 CONC de Corneilles).  
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Adelaide de Barcelona was married seigneur de Tosni et Conches Roger de Tosny I, son of seigneur de Tosni et Conches Ralph de Tosny II. Later she married Richard, 2nd comte d' Évereux, son of Robert, archevêque de Rouen et comte d
2 CONC ' Évereux and Herleve de Normandie, circa 1041.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide de Barcelona died in 1051 at the age of 47 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"  ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p343.htm#i5264 )  from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT --------------------
