2 CONT Ramiro Sánchez of Monzón (1070 - 1116) was a noble kinsman of the kings of Navarre, and lord of the town of Monzón, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was Sancho Garcés, an illegitimate son of king García Sánchez III of Navarre. His mother was Constance, whose parentage has been subject to recent speculation - associated with the lords of Marañon in traditional source
2 CONC s, she has lately been suggested to have been daughter of queen Estefanía, King García's wife, and hence stepsister of her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT With the fall of his uncle, king Sancho IV of Navarre, the kingdom was divided between Castile and Aragon, and the royal family parceled out between the two. Ramiro was thus raised at the Aragonese court, and was lord of Monzón, i
2 CONC n which we was succeeded by his eldest son, the future king García Ramírez of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramiro was married to Cristina Rodríguez, daughter of Rodrigo Díaz de Vivar, El Cid.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see: Kings of Navarre family tree
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Children García Ramírez of Navarre (The Restorer King), King of Navarre  Alfonso, sn de Castroviejo  Estefania, wife of Count Fruela Díaz  Elvira, wife of count Rodrigo Gómez and mother of Gonzalo Ruiz of Bureba 
