1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A'isha bint Mu`awiya ben al-Mughira1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 630
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Mu`awiya ben al-Mughira1 b. circa 600
2 CONT
2 CONT      'A'isha bint Mu`awiya ben al-Mughira was born circa 630. She was the daughter of Mu`awiya ben al-Mughira.1 'A'isha bint Mu`awiya ben al-Mughira married Marwân I ibn al-Hakam al-Qurayshi, 4th Umayyad Caliph, son of al-Hakim ib
2 CONC n Abûl 'Âs and Amina bint `Alkama al-Kinaniyya, before 646.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Marwân I ibn al-Hakam al-Qurayshi, 4th Umayyad Caliph b. 623, d. 685
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwân, 5th Umayyad Caliph+ b. c 646, d. Oct 7051
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S187] Royal Genealogy Database, online http://www.dcs.hull.ac.uk/public/genealogy/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwan_I
2 CONT
2 CONT He was popularly known as Marwan I. He had known the Islamic prophet Muhammad and is thus considered a companion, and served as the secretary and right-hand man of his kinsman, the Caliph, Uthman Affan al-Umayyah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marwan had at least sixteen children, among them at least twelve sons from five wives and an umm walad (concubine).[6] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A'isha bint Muʿawiya ibn al-Mughira was the first wife of Marwan ibn al-Ḥakam ibn Abi al-ʿAs ibn Umayya (abt 623-685), who was the fourth caliph of the Umayyad dynasty (reigned 684–685) [1] and the first of the Marwanid caliphs. [
2 CONC 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT From his wife A'isha, a daughter of his paternal first cousin Mu'awiya ibn al-Mughira, he had his eldest son Abd al-Malik, Mu'awiya and daughter Umm Amr.[6][7] Umm Amr later married Sa'id ibn Khalid ibn Amr, a great-grandson of Ma
2 CONC rwan's paternal first cousin Uthman ibn Affan, who became caliph (leader of the Muslim community) in 644.[8] 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Given name also shown as '''Aisha''', '''Aminah''' and '''Amina'''
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to [http://www.geni.com/people/Marw%C3%A2n-I-bin-al-Hakam/6000000003153451632/ '''Marwân I bin al-Hakam'''], the son of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/al-Hakam-bin-Abu-al-%CA%BBAs/6000000003493135478/ al-Hakam bin 
2 CONC Abu al-ʻAs]'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many Western sources call 'Aisha a daughter of the Prophet Muhammad's daughter Ruqayyah. However, Ruqayyah had only one known child, a son named 'Abd-allâh who died at the age of 6. These sources are based on later Umayyid propaga
2 CONC nda that claimed a descent from Muhammad for the Umayidd caliphs. The Umayidd claim was rejected by other descendants of Muhammad. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Arab sources identify her as a daughter of Uthman's Christian wife, Nayla bint Farasa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family_tree_of_Uthman
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 2: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uthman_ibn_Affan
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 3: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwan_ibn_al-Hakam
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 4: http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~dearbornboutwell/fam1783.html
