1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berenguer Renard de Peralada
2 CONT
2 CONT Berenguer Renard de Peralada or Carmençó was perhaps Viscount of Rocabertí , what he was was lord of Peralada . He was probably the son and heir of Viscount Dalmau III of Rocabertí , and although he had descendants, it will not la
2 CONC st and all the patrimony passed to his possible brother Jofre I of Rocabertí with whom begins the safe lineage of the Viscounts of Rocabertí.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Gausbert de Peralada Perhaps it had the descendants that are detailed next of a lady who is not known to us:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gausbert de Peralada, lord of Peralada and died in 1132 Ramon de Torrelles or de Peralada, lord of Peralada, died in 1176 Eimeric de Torrelles or de Peralada, lord of Peralda and also died in 1176 Dalmau (?) Canon of Girona
2 CONT
2 CONT List of viscounts of Rocabertí: [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT First lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dalmau I of Rocabertí (a. 971-d. 985) viscount of Peralada and viscount of Rocabertí (?) Dalmau II de Rocabertí (d. 985-d. 1017) viscount of Peralada William I of Rocabertí (d. 1017-d.1058) = Bonadona Ramon Guillem I de Rocabertí 
2 CONC (d. 1058-c. 1090) viscount of Peralada , viscount of Verges and viscount of Rocabertí Arsenda de Rocabertí (c. 1090-c. 1110) = Berenguer d'Empúries or Berenguer Renard de Quermançó Second lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dalmau (III) de Rocabertí [o de Quermançó] (circa 1110-a. 1131) [ viscount of Peralada ] and viscount of Rocabertí , son of Berenguer d'Empúries and Arsenda [of Rocabertí] Berenguer Renard de Peralada (a. 1131-a. 1132) Gausbert de
2 CONC  Peralada (b. 1132-c. 1138) Jofre (I) de Rocabertí (circa 1138-1166) Dalmau (IV) de Rocabertí (1166-1181) Jofre (II) de Rocabertí (1181-1212)
2 CONT
2 CONT Shield of the Rocabertí in the castle of Peralada , already with the count's crown Dalmau (V) de Rocabertí (1212-1229) Hug Jofre (I) de Rocabertí (1229-1250) [regent] Jofre (III) de Rocabertí (1229 / 1250-1282) Dalmau (VI) of Roca
2 CONC bertí and Palau (1282-1304) Jofre (IV) de Rocabertí i Desfar (1304-1309) Dalmau (VII) of Rocabertí and Urgell (1309-1324) Jofre (V) of Rocabertí and Serrallonga (1324-1342) Felip Dalmau (I) of Rocabertí and Montcada (1342-1392) Jo
2 CONC fre (VI) of Rocabertí and Fenollet (1392-1403) Dalmau (VIII) by Rocabertí and Ferrandis d'Híxar (1403-1454) Jofre (VII) of Rocabertí and Montcada (1454-1479) Felip Dalmau (II) de Rocabertí i de Castre-Pinós (1479-1512) Martí Onofr
2 CONC e (I) de Rocabertí i de Rocabertí (1512-1567) Francesc Dalmau I de Rocabertí i de Sarriera (1567-1592) Francesc Jofre I de Rocabertí i de Pacs (1592-1634) count of Peralada in 1599 Francesc Dalmau II of Rocabertí and Safortesa (16
2 CONC 34-1644) Ramon Dalmau I of Rocabertí and Safortesa (1644-1663) Marquis of Anglesola in 1645 Martí Jofre I de Rocabertí i de Safortesa (1663-1671) Elisenda I de Rocabertí i de Safortesa (1671-d 1672) = Ramon de Rocafull-Puixmarín ,
2 CONC  comte d'Albatera
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  The ordinal numbering of the viscounts varies according to the historiographic traditions. Here we follow the one established by the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana (with corrections of obvious errors) and not the one used previous
2 CONC ly by Santiago Sobrequés , who did not count the members of the first Rocabertí lineage, to consider them viscounts of Peralada , and who counts as in Jofre (III) the Viscount Hug Jofre (I).
