1 NOTE Ermengarde of Anjou (c. 1018 - 18 March 1076), daughter of Count Fulk III of Anjou and Hildegarde was born in Angers, and was murdered at the Church of Fleurey-sur-Ouche, Côte-d'Or[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT From her first marriage to Geoffrey, Count of Gâtinais she had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hildegarde de Château-Landon 
2 CONT Geoffrey III, Count of Anjou 
2 CONT Fulk IV, Count of Anjou 
2 CONT From her second marriage to Robert I, Duke of Burgundy she had one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hildegard (c. 1056-1104), married Duke William VIII of Aquitaine 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT ^ http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANJOU,%20MAINE.htm#ErmengardeM1GeoffroyIIGatinaisM2RobertIA 
