1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#HumbertGrenobledied1030<br/>
2 CONT 1.         HUMBERT ([960/70]-[after 1030]).  "Humbertus episcopus Gratianopolitanensis" donated property "medietatem castri de Visilia" to Cluny by charter dated [Sep/Oct] 996, subscribed by "Fredeburgis matris eius, Wiguonis frat
2 CONC ris eius, Humberti episcopi de Valentia nepotis eius"[156].  His birth date range is estimated on the assumption that he was adult when appointed to his bishopric.  '''Bishop of Grenoble''' 990 or before.  "Wigo et uxor mea Fredeb
2 CONC urga" donated property "in comitatu Viennensi in agro Cassiacensi in villa…Vernio" by charter dated Sep [996], subscribed by "Umberti episcopi, Richardi, Vagoni, Bosoni, Adraldi"[157].  "Umbertus Grationopolensis ecclesiæ præsul" 
2 CONC donated property "locum de Sancto Bartholomeo cum ecclesia de Madernatis" to the abbey of Saint-Chaffre with the consent of "Radulfo rege et regina Ermengarda, et domino archiepiscopo Brocardo, matre quoque mea Fredeburge, atque M
2 CONC aileno nepote meo, simulque aliis nepotibus meis Umberto atque Wigone" by charter dated 1012, signed by "Fredeburgæ matris eius, Wigonis et Umberti filiorum fratris eius, Malleni nepotis eius"[158].  Prudhomme states that Bishop H
2 CONC umbert was still living in 1030 but had abandoned the administration of his diocesis to his nephew Mallen[159].  He cites no primary source to support his statement.  
