2 CONT ** 2. '''AUDEBERT''' [III] (-before Feb 1168). "Aldebertus comes, filius…Aalmodis comitissæ, frater Bosonis" confirmed his mother’s donation referred to above by charter dated 7 Apr 1113, witnessed by "Almodis comitissa mater Alde
2 CONC berti…"[106]. A charter dated to [1124/29] relating to a dispute between the abbé de Charroux and the abbesse de Fontevrault refers to a previous donation with the consent of "Almodi comitissa Charofensi ac filius eius Audeberto e
2 CONC t Bosone"[107]. The Chronicle of Saint-Maxence records that "Rotgerio comite" & his wife had two sons[108]. "Odo comes" donated property to Tulle, with the consent of "fratre meo Aldeberto", by charter dated to [1106][109]. '''Com
2 CONC te de la Marche'''. '''m ORENGARDE''', daughter of ---. The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified. 1145. 
2 CONT ** '''Audebert [III] & his wife had three children:'''
2 CONT *** a) '''AUDEBERT''' [IV] (-Constantinople 29 Aug 1178, or 1180, or 7 Oct 1187, bur "Barbeu")....'''Comte de la Marche''' 1145....'''m''' (repudiated) as her first husband, '''MIRABLE''', daughter of ---.  The primary source whic
