1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AQUITAINE%20NOBILITY.htm#GuyKingJerusalemdied1194
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_VII_of_Lusignan
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh VII the Brown of Lusignan or Hugues II de La Marche or Hugues VII & II le Brun de Lusignan (1065 – 1151), Sire de Lusignan, Couhé and Château-Larcher and Count of La Marche, was the son of Hugh VI of Lusignan. He was one of t
2 CONC he many notable Crusaders in the Lusignan family. In 1147 he took the Cross and followed King Louis VII of France on the Second Crusade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh married before 1109 Sarrasine or Saracena de Lezay (1067 – 1144), whose origins are unknown. She may have been identical to the Saracena who was widow of Robert I, Count of Sanseverino. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hugh VIII of Lusignan  
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. William de Lusignan, Seigneur d'Angles  
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Rorgon de Lusignan  
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Simon I de Lusignan, Seigneur de Lezay, fl. 1144, married before 1173 NN
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Galeran de Lusignan 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Ænor or Aénor de Lusignan (b. c. 1130), married before 1144 Geoffrey or Geoffroy V de Thouars (c. 1120 – aft. 1176), Vicomte de Thouars, son of Aimery VI de Thouars, Vicomte de Thouars, and wife Agnes=Mathilde de Poitiers
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon I was the father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT a. Guillaume I de Lusignan, Seigneur de Lezay, who died unmarried and without issue and
2 CONT
2 CONT b. Simon II de Lusignan (Deux Sevres, bef. 1180 – 1200), Seigneur de Lezay, married before 1195 NN. They were the parents of Hugues I de Lezay, Seigneur de Lezay, who was the father of Jean I de Lezay, Seigneur de Lezay, who was t
2 CONC he father of Claire I de Lezay, Dame de Lezay, married to Pons II d'Aulnay, Vicomte d'Aulnay.
