2 CONT
2 CONT Emma de Mortain de Toulouse (c.1058-), daughter of Robert of Cornwall and Mathilde of Montgomerry, wife of William IV of Toulouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, Count of Mortain
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was married to Matilda, daughter of Roger de Montgomerie, 1st Earl of Shrewsbury, and by her left a son, the aforementioned William of Mortain, and three daughters; Agnes who married André de Vitry, Denise, married in 1078 
2 CONC to Guy, 3rd Sire de La Val; and Emma of Mortain, the wife of William IV of Toulouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William IV of Toulouse
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT William IV of Toulouse was married to Emma of Mortain (daughter of Robert, Count of Mortain and a niece of William of Normandy), who gave him one daughter, Philippa.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Emma of Mortain was the daughter of Robert Count of Mortain and Matilda de Montgomery. Her married name was Toulouse. Emma of Mortain married William IV Count of Toulouse, son of Pons Count of Toulouse, in 1080. Emma of Mortain di
2 CONC ed in 1093
