2 CONC harter dated 26 Feb 1020 under which “Fredenandus Flayniz et eius coniuge Geloire” donated property to the monks of San Martín. “...Pelagio Froyla...Xemenio Froylan...” confirmed the charter dated 26 Feb 1022 under which Alfonso V
2 CONC  King of León set the limits of hunting rights at Santa María de Obona. “...Petrus Froilaz, Pelagius Froilaz...” confirmed the charter dated 2 Aug 1026 under which "Didacus Fredenandiz et uxor mea Marina et filiis nostris" donated
2 CONC  "Uilla Reuelle...in Ualle de Ratario...hereditate que fecit Uincenti ad Fafila Olaliz avius istius Didaco Fredenandiz" to León Cathedral. "…Pelagio Froilaz…" subscribed the charter dated 15 Nov 1028 under which "Ueremudus proles 
2 CONC Adefonsi principis et Geluire regine" donated "villam meam…Cordario que fuit avorum et parentum meorum Menendi et dne Tote" to Santiago de Compostela.
