2 TITL Belmonte-de-Mirand
2 NOTE https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelayo_Froilaz_el_Diácono
3 CONT In 1014, already married to Countess Aldonza Ordóñez, Pelayo Froilaz appears with his wife's family in the documentation of the disappeared monastery of Lapedo in Belmonte de Miranda and shortly after in a diploma in the cathedral
3 CONC  of San Salvador de Oviedo with his mother-in-law, Cristina Bermúdez confirming how Pelagius Froilaz eats. He was royal ensign of King Alfonso V of León from 1016 to 1019 and a member of the royal curia where his presence is recor
3 CONC ded confirming royal diplomas in 1023 and 1026. Shortly after and before 1030 it already appears with the title of count.[ 6]
3 CONT
3 CONT With his wife Aldonza he founded the monastery of Lapedo, now disappeared, in Belmonte de Miranda where they probably received burial. The date of his death is not known but it must have occurred after 1048 and close to the death 
3 CONC of his wife who was still alive in 1050.[ 6]
2 NOTE https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belmonte-de-Miranda.jpg
