2 CONT ** 4. https://mercaba.org/SANTORAL/Vida/03/03-01_san_rosendo.htm Tradition runs as follows: "The countess was not sterile. But her children died, newborns. Once Count Don Gutierre left on the expedition of Don Alfonso III against 
2 CONC Coimbra, Ilduara, his wife, came to pray in this valley. While he was here One morning, she went up to the hermitage of San Salvador, alone and barefoot, and crying. She arrived very tired. Even so, she immediately began to pray. 
2 CONC Very devoted to San Miguel, she first prostrated herself before his altar. There she remained for a long time Suddenly, he heard a voice that said to him: "Rejoice, Ilduara, that your prayer has been answered. Behold, you will con
2 CONC ceive and give birth to a son who will be great before God and men." And it happened just as the archangel prophesied. He planned to baptize the child in San Salvador. But, when some carters went up the mountain with the parish ba
2 CONC ptismal font, their cart broke down. They went to look for another. And, meanwhile, San Miguel took the font to his hermitage The countess understood that, with that task, the angel wanted to indicate his desire that the child be 
2 CONC baptized in the new church, and so she ordered her family to do so. They named him Rosendo. All this happened at the end of the ninth century or early ten". …. The birth took place on November 26, 907. The baptism, a few days. In 
2 CONC it, Sabarico, the newborn's uncle, acted as baptizer. On such an occasion the nobility congratulated the counts. All the settlers celebrated. The slaves, who received their freedom that day, jumped for joy. There was general rejoi
2 CONC cing. Don Gutierre, in thanksgiving, without leaving his position, dedicated himself from then on to founding monasteries and rebuilding churches. Skillful ruler and pious Christian, he passed on to his son the rich legacy of his 
2 CONC robust character. Doña Ilduara, for her part, was endowing the churches and monasteries that her husband built, with estates, with vestments, with sacred vessels. Noble and detached, fervent and holy, she deserved the prize that t
2 CONC he heavenly messenger prophesied for her: "a great son before God and men."
2 CONT ** 6. Patron Saints Index: Saint Rudesind < [https://web.archive.org/web/20051216103158/http://catholicforum.com/saints/saintr1h.htm link] >
