2 CONT '''m''' secondly (before 1 Nov 1106) '''ALMODIS''', daughter of --- (-[23 Nov 1111/3 Feb 1112]).  "Raymundus comes Barchinonensis" donated all that he had captured at Balagario to "uxori mea Almodis et filiis quos de ea habuero" b
2 CONC y charter dated 1 Nov 1106[396].  Her parentage is not known.  A charter dated 26 Sep 1110 records that Ramon Berenguer was still childless by his marriage at that date[397].  "Raimundis Berengarii…marchio Barchionensium, princeps
2 CONC  Ausonensium, comes vero Gerundensium atque Bisullunensium" donated property "ecclesiam Sancte Marie intra muros Bisullunensis" to Valence Saint-Rufus by charter dated 23 Nov 1111, signed by "Raimundi comitis, Meltis comitisse"[39
2 CONC 8]. 
