1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''''
2 CONT ==Archimbaud ll Le Blanc de Macon==
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT - Viscount of Macon.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Known in Siena as Macone, was elected Consol in Siena in 1168 and 1169.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In the opinion of "Enciclopedia Dantesca"     (http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/maconi_%28Enciclopedia-Dantesca%29/) is named "Macone di Paganello", but Paganello was not the father name, but the appellative is due to the latin
2 CONC  name of his french fief "Pagus Matisconensis" aka Macon
2 CONT perhaps the italian vulgar diminutive of "Pagus" was "Paganellus" and this is due to the fact that Archimbaud ll of Macon was the viscount and not the count of Macon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Always in the opinion of "Enciclopedia Dantesca" ( http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/maconi_%28Enciclopedia-Dantesca%29/) Macone was an offspring of the Family of the counts Ugurgieri of the Berardenga, but this opinion is incor
2 CONC rect because in 1163 the family name "Ugurgieri" did not exist yet, in fact in the list of Siena's Consules "Ugo Ruggeri - Hugues son of Roger" (Hugues was forefather of the Ugurgeri Family) is posterior to the year 1168 enough (y
2 CONC ear 1192), however the hypothesis of a familiar relationship is plausible for two reasons:  - both the families were of Carolingian offspring; - the two families lived in Siena in contiguous palacies in the "Terzo of San Martino" 
2 CONC (source: " Caleffo Vecchio").
