2 CONC  at Fontevraud Abbey, always charming to men, pleasing to God, and like an angel." Her son from her first marriage was Fulk V of Anjou who later became King of Jerusalem iure uxoris. The dynasties founded by Fulk's sons ruled for 
2 CONC centuries, one of them in England (Plantagenet), the other in Jerusalem.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Bertrade de Montfort was the daughter of Simon I de Montfort and Agnes, Countess of Evereaux.
2 CONT
2 CONT She first married Fulk IV, Count of Anjou having a son named Fulk of Jerusalem.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married second, Philip I of France and had:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Philip of France, Count of Mantes (living in 1123)
2 CONT * Fleury of France, Seigneur of Nangis (living in 1118)
2 CONT * Cecile of France (died 1145) These were her only marriages and only children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Any inconsistencies are due to erroneous merging of trees by multiple Geni-users. There were a couple Bertrade's with fathers named Simon who were merged. They were of 2 different generations, thus causing multiple errors with chi
2 CONC ldren, husbands and close family members. This shall be fixed soon.
2 CONT
