1 OCCU Knight Templar, Comte d'Anjou, Comte de Tours (vv.1109-1129), Comte du Maine (vv.1110-1129), Roi de Jérusalem (vv.1131-1143)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulk,_King_of_Jerusalem ''[41 languages]''
2 CONT '''Fulk of Anjou '''(Latin: ''Fulco'', French: ''Foulque'' or ''Foulques''; c. 1089/1092 – 13 November 1143), also known as '''Fulk the Younger''', was the king of Jerusalem from 1131 until 1143 as the husband and co-ruler of Quee
2 CONC n Melisende. Previously, he was the count of Anjou as '''Fulk V''' from 1109 to 1129. He had also been the count of Maine from 1110 to 1126 alongside his first wife, Countess Erembourg. His direct descendants were the rulers of th
2 CONC e Angevin Empire and the Latin Kingdom of Jerusalem. .. ... .... .....
2 CONT
