1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Gotelana de Clerieux 
2 CONT * AKA De Clerieu
2 CONT * Sex: F 
2 CONT * Birth: Abt 971 in Clerieu, France 
2 CONT * Father: Silvion De CLERIEU b: Abt 941 
2 CONT * Mother: Willa De CLERIEU b: Abt 941 
2 CONT * Marriage 1 Guiges D'ALBON b: Abt 970 in Albon, Rhone Alpes, France - Married: Bef 18 Oct 1013  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT #Guigues D'ALBON b: 995 in Albon, Rhone Alpes, France.  Guigues I Vetus, Comte d'Albon   d. 22 Apr 1075, Cluny (as a monk).  Married 1) Adelais de Turin 2) Inez of Barcelona 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#GuiguesIdied1075B
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         GUIGUES [II] (-[1009]).  "…Wiguonis fratris eius…" subscribed the charter dated [Sep/Oct] 996 under which "Humbertus episcopus Gratianopolitanensis" donated property to Cluny[162].  m [GOTELENE, daughter of ---.  It is 
2 CONC possible that the wife of Guigues [II] was Gotelene if the charter under which "Wigo comes filius Gotelenne" donated "ecclesiam de Visilia" to Cluny refers to Guigues [III] "Vetus"[163].  Europäische Stammtafeln names her "Gotelan
2 CONC a de Clérieux", but assigns her as the wife of Guigues [III] "Vetus/Vieux"[164].  No doubt this hypothesis is based on a different interpretation of the same charter.  The basis for ''Europäische Stammtafeln'' suggesting that Gote
2 CONC lana was "de Clérieux" has not yet been found.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Guigues [II] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         HUMBERT ([995/1000]-[1037]). … Bishop of Valence .  
2 CONT * b)         GUIGUES [III] "Vetus/Vieux" ([995/1000]-Cluny 22 Apr [1074/75]). Comte d’Albon.  -        see below.  
2 CONT * c)         GUILLAUME (-7 Nov [1012]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Silvion I x Willa :
2 CONT
2 CONT Silvion agit de sa propre autorité et en présence de son épouse Guille dès 973. Il est donc né vers 950 peut-être un peu plus tôt pour une chronologie fluide.
2 CONT
2 CONT Silvion et Willa ont eu pour enfants :
2 CONT # Guillaume qui suit ;
2 CONT # Adon (d’après Gallier p 286) ;
2 CONT # Gothelène x Guigues d’Albon l’ancien d’où Guigues cousin germain de l’évêque de Vienne Léger (CSB n° 277 et 56). Vers 1090, Guigues fils de Gothelène fait une donation à Saint André le Bas (CSAB [19] n° 64).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000221452291934&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://thierryhelene.bianco.free.fr/drupal/?q=node/137
2 CONT # Le 28 août 973 ?, Sylvion et son épouse Willa, pour obtenir le pardon de leurs péchés donnent à l'église de Roman... un manse à Chanos (villa cannoscho).... (RD n° 1340 et CSB n° 259).
2 CONT # Quelques années plus tard, Sylvion réapparait pour une nouvelle donation : en 976 ou 977, donation au monastère de Cluny par Sylvion, son épouse Wille et leur fils Guillaume de biens au pagus de Viviers pour la fondation d’un pr
2 CONC ieuré à Saint Pierre du Rompon (CLU [18] n°1434).
2 CONT # https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00048717&tree=LEO cites 
2 CONT ## [S00301] Schwennicke, Detlev (Ed.), ~Europäische Stammtafeln, J.A. Stargardt Verlag, Marburg. 3/4:738 
2 CONT # http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#GuiguesIdied1075B. Prudhomme distinguishes two individuals in place of "Guigues [III]"[190].  He states that the older Guigues died in 1034, married "Gotelenne", and that his son was
2 CONC  the second person, Guigues "Vetus".  He cites no primary source in support of his theory, in particular no document which indicates that one of the counts Guigues died in 1034.  The division of this person into two seems unnecess
2 CONC ary to explain the primary sources.  The family relationships shown in this document leave no primary source reference unexplained.  In any case, it seems appropriate that Guigues "Vetus" should be identified with Guigues [III] as
2 CONC  he would have well merited his nickname, assuming that his birth date is correctly estimated as shown above. 
