2 CONT  Fortanier de Mauriac
2 CONT
2 CONT This noble haunt belonged to very powerful families of Perigord; As soon as The year 1000, Fortanier de Mauriac is the lord and then the castle passes to the hands of the Taillefer, counts of Perigord, by marriage of Fine de Mauri
2 CONC ac. It later became the property of the Of Lagut, of the Grimoards; Then at the beginning of the eighteenth century, it failed the Talleyrand and remained Their property until the Revolution. At the end of the 19th century, the Vi
2 CONC comte de la Besges owner. Today it is owned by Mr. Dumoncel. This beautiful castle of Mauriac is inscribed in the supplementary inventory of Monuments Historical since 1948-
2 CONT
