2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id50.html '''Ancient Welsh Studies “Welsh Origins of the Peverel Family”''']
2 CONT
2 CONT The extant pedigrees identify a wife of "William Peverel" as Oddona, daughter of Earl Hugh Avranches[9]; she is usually cited as a second wife of William the Younger but such a lady would occur c. 1060 and the marriage probably be
2 CONC longs to a William born nearer 1050 than 1080.  We assign it to the son of Ranulph named William of Dover.  The youngest brother of Hamo and William was Payne who is also said to have died without male issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of William fitz Ranulph, we believe, was also named Payne and born c. 1080.  He married a "de Metz" lady who was probably a daughter of Warin the Bald de Metz and sister of the first Fulk fitzWarin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Welsh Origins of the Peverel Family; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id50.html. (Steven Ferry, April 15, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Dictionary_of_National_Biography,_1885-1900/Peverell,_William '''Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900 Volume 45 "Peverell, William"''']
