2 CONC of La Marche on his father's death in 1151. Born in Poitou, 1106-1110 or some time after 1125, he died in Holy Land in 1165 or 1171. He married in 1140/1141 Bourgogne or Burgondie de Rancon, Dame de Fontenay, daughter of Geoffroi 
2 CONC or Geoffroy de Rancon, Seigneur de Taillebourg and wife Fossefie=Falsifie, Dame de Moncontour, by whom he also became Seigneur de Fontenay: she died in April 11, 1169. In 1163 or 1164 he went on pilgrimage and on crusade to the Ho
