1 OCCU Seigneur de Montpellier, Senhor de Montpellier, Lord of Montpellier
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_V_of_Montpellier
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William V or Guilhem V (1075 – 1121)''' was the Lord of Montpellier from an early age until his death. He was the son of Bernard William IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon after his father's death, his mother, Ermengarde, quit Montpellier to marry the Lord of Anduze. William IV had confided the tutelage of his son to the child's grandmother, Beliarde, and to his nearest relatives: William Arnol
2 CONC d, Raymond Stephen, and William Aymoin. After a short conflict with the bishop of Maguelonne, William V rendered homage to the bishop on 10 December 1090 and was recognised as lord of Montpellier.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the calle of Pope Urban II, William took up the cross of the First Crusade under the banner of Raymond IV of Toulouse. He served notable at the capture of the small Syrian village of Maara in 1098. After the fall of Jerusalem i
2 CONC n 1099, William remained in the Holy Land for a while. He remained at the side of Godfrey de Bouillon and accompanied him to the Battle of Arsuf in December. He did not return to Montpellier until 1103, bringing with him a relic o
2 CONC f Saint Cleopas.
2 CONT
2 CONT When William returned, he found that the Aimoin brothers to whom he had confided the administration of the lordship in his absence had usurped many seigniorial rights and that he was obligated to recognise much of their newfound a
2 CONC uthority, which diminished his own, in order to retain his position.
2 CONT
2 CONT William participated in the army of Raymond Berengar III of Barcelona which captured Majorca from the Moors in 1114. The rest of his reign was marked by the important acquisition of nearby territories, which greatly recouped his p
2 CONC ower: Montarnaud, Cournonsec, Montferrier, Frontignan, Aumelas, Montbazin, Popian.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to Ermensenda, daughter of the Peter, Count of Mauguio, he had six children:
2 CONT # William VI 
2 CONT # William, Lord of Aumelas 
2 CONT # Bernard, Lord of Villeneuve 
2 CONT # Guillelme, married Raymon Bernard, Count of Mauguio 
2 CONT # Ermeniarde 
2 CONT # Adelaide
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Contributeurs à Wikipedia, 'Guilhem V de Montpellier', Wikipédia, l'encyclopédie libre, 12 janvier 2011, 19:46 UTC, <http://fr.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Guilhem_V_de_Montpellier&oldid=61217206> [Page consultée le 16 février 
2 CONC 2011]
2 CONT
2 CONT Guilhem V (1075 - 1121), fils de Bernard Guilhem IV, Seigneurie de Montpellier et d'Aumelas.
2 CONT  Il est très jeune à la mort de son père. Sa mère, Ermengarde, quitte Montpellier peu de temps après pour épouser le seigneur d' Anduze. Bernard Guilhem IV avait confié la garde de l'enfant à sa grand-mère Beliarde ainsi qu'à des 
2 CONC proches parents, Guilhem Arnaud, Raimond Etienne et Guilhem Aymoin.
2 CONT  À la suite d'un conflit avec l'évêque de Maguelone, Guilhem V lui prête serment de fidélité le 10 décembre 1090 et reconnaît tenir de lui Montpellier.
2 CONT  À l'appel du pape Urbain II, il prend la croix et participe à la première croisade sous la bannière du comte Raymond IV de Toulouse. Il s'illustre notamment lors de la prise de la petite ville syrienne de Maara en 1098. Après la 
2 CONC prise de Jérusalem, Guilhem V, contrairement à de nombreux seigneurs, ne va pas quitter la Terre Sainte tout de suite. Il reste aux côté de Godefroy de Bouillon, devenu roi de Jérusalem qui tente d'affermir les conquêtes franques,
2 CONC  ilots isolés en terres musulmanes. Il l'accompagne en décembre 1099 au siège d'Arsuf qui est un échec.
2 CONT  En 1103, Guilhem V est de retour à Montpellier, rapportant de Terre Sainte une relique de saint Cléophas. Ayant confié l'administration de la seigneurie de Montpellier aux viguiers, les frères Aimoins (qui en ont profité pour usu
2 CONC rper de nombreux droits), il doit s'entendre avec eux et est obligé de démembrer son autorité seigneuriale.
2 CONT  Il participe à la prise de Majorque sur les Maures en 1114 aux côtés du comte Raimond-Bérenger III de Barcelone.
2 CONT  Le reste de son règne est marqué par des acquisitions importantes (Montarnaud, Cournonsec, Montferrier, Frontignan, Aumelas, Montbazin, Popian).
2 CONT  Marié à Ermensende en 1087, fille du comte de Melgueil, dont sont issus:
2 CONT  Sibylle de Montpellier qui aurait épousé Bernard III d'Anduze vers 1110.
2 CONT  Guillemette de Montpellier (Ou Guillelme), qui épousera Bernard de Melgueil.
2 CONT  Guilhem VI de Montpellier qui épousera en 1129 Sybille de Saluces
2 CONT  Guilhem d'Aumelas, minor, qui sera le second mari de Thiburge d'Orange.
2 CONT  Bernard, seigneur de Villeneuve
2 CONT  Adelaïs de Montpellier (Alix,Adelaïde), née vers 1136 au Château de Gallargues, qui sera en 1151 la seconde épouse d'Ebles III de Ventadour.
2 CONT  Ermeniarde de Montpellier, née en 1106.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In English:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Guilhem V (1075 - 1121), son of Bernard IV Guilhem ,Lord of Montpellier and Aumelas.
2 CONT  He is very young at the death of his father. His mother, Ermengarde, Montpellier leaves shortly after marrying the lord of Anduze . Guilhem Bernard IV had awarded custody of the child to his grandmother Beliard as well as relativ
2 CONC es, Guilhem Arnaud, Etienne and Raymond Guilhem Aymoin.
2 CONT  Following a dispute with the Bishop of Maguelone , Guilhem V he takes the oath of fidelity December 10, 1090 recognizes and hold him Montpellier.
2 CONT  At the urging of Pope Urban II , he took the cross and took part in the first crusade under the banner of Count Raymond IV of Toulouse . He particularly distinguished himself during the capture of the Syrian town of Maara in 1098
2 CONC . After the capture of Jerusalem , Guilhem V, unlike many lords, will not leave the Holy Land immediately. It remains next to Godfrey of Bouillon , who became king of Jerusalem who attempts to strengthen the Frankish conquest, isl
2 CONC ets isolated in Muslim lands. He accompanies him in December 1099 at the headquarters of Arsuf is a failure.
2 CONT  In 1103, Guilhem V is back in Montpellier, referring to the Holy Land a relic of Saint Cleophas. Having entrusted the administration of the lordship of Montpellier to provosts, brothers Aimoin (who took the opportunity to usurp m
2 CONC any of the rights), it must agree with them and is forced to dismember his lordly authority.
2 CONT  He participates in decision- Mallorca from the Moors in 1114 alongside Count Raimond Berenger III, Barcelona .
2 CONT  The rest of his reign was marked by significant acquisitions ( Montarnaud , Cournonsec , Montferrier , Frontignan , Aumelas , Montbazin , Popian ).
2 CONT  Married to Ermensende in 1087, daughter of Count Melgueil 1 , from which come two :
2 CONT  Sibylle de Montpellier who married Bernard Anduze III in 1110 3 .
2 CONT  Guillemette de Montpellier (Or Guillelme ), who married Bernard Melgueil .
2 CONT  Guilhem VI of Montpellier in 1129 who married Sybille of Saluzzo
2 CONT  Guilhem Aumelas , minor , who will be the second husband Thiburge Orange 4 .
2 CONT  Bernard, Lord of Villeneuve 5
2 CONT  Adela de Montpellier ( Alix , Adelaide ) was born circa 1136 at Castle Gallargues , which in 1151 will be the second wife of Ebles Ventadour III .
2 CONT  Ermeniarde Montpellier , born in 1106 6 .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Personnages des Croisades: Premième Croisade (1096-1099)==
2 CONT [http://www.templiers.net/personnages-croisades/index.php?page=personnages_croisade_1#0476]
2 CONT
2 CONT "'''Guillaume V, seigneur de Montpellie'''r, donna tous ses biens à l'église de Maguelonne avant de partir pour la Terre-Sainte. D. Vaissète raconte ses nombreux exploits contre les Sarrazins, et lui donna pour armes, d'après d'an
2 CONC ciens sceaux: d'argent, au tourteau de gueules."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guillaume V, lord of Montpellier,''' gave all his possessions to the church of Maguelonne before leaving for the Holy Land. D. Vaissète recounts his many exploits against the Saracens, and gave him for arms, according to ancien
2 CONC t seals: Argent, cake Gules."
