2 CONT William X (1099 – 9 April 1137), called the Saint, was Duke of Aquitaine, Duke of Gascony, and Count of Poitou (as William VIII) between 1126 and 1137. He was the son of William IX by his second wife, Philippa of Toulouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born in Toulouse during the brief period when his parents ruled the capital. His birth is recorded in the Chronicle of Saint-Maixent for the year 1099: Willelmo comiti natus est filius, equivoce Guillelmus vocatus ("a 
2 CONC son was born to Count William, named William like himself"). Later that same year, much to his wife's ire, Duke William mortgaged Toulouse to Philippa's cousin, Bertrand of Toulouse, and then left on Crusade.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Royal Family - Ramnulfids
2 CONT Father	William IX, Duke of Aquitaine Mother	Philippa of Toulouse Born	1099 Toulouse Died	9 April 1137
