1 OCCU Duchess of Burgundy, Countess of Burgundy, Countess consort of Ponthieu 1115 - Feb. 28, 1141, AKA "Helie of Burgundy"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Alix de Bourgogne) (Alice de Bourgogne) (Adélaïde de Bourgogne) Helie of Burgundy seems to get mixed up with a different Alice or Allix of Burgundy. This Helie is the daughter of Odo (Eudes) I of Burgundy and Siby
2 CONC lla of Burgundy. She married Bertrand of Toulouse/Tripoli and William III of Ponthieu
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helie_of_Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Helie of Burgundy (c.1080 – 28 February 1141) was the daughter of Eudes I and Sibylla of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1095, she married Bertrand de Toulouse, as his second wife. The two had one son, Pons de Tripoli (c.1098–1137).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrand succeeded his father as Count of Toulouse in 1105, and in 1108, he set out for Outremer to claim his father's rights as Count of Tripoli. Helie accompanied him on this expedition, which resulted in the capture of Tripoli 
2 CONC in 1109; shortly after, their nephew, William-Jordan died of wounds, giving Bertrand an undisputed claim to Tripoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrand died in 1112, and Pons succeeded him in Tripoli. Helie returned to France, where she married William III of Ponthieu in 1115. They had twelve children, including two named Robert, two named William, and two named Enguerra
2 CONC nd:
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy II of Ponthieu (d. 1147)
2 CONT
2 CONT William (d. aft. 1166)
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Garennes (d. aft. 1171), a monk
2 CONT
2 CONT William Enguerrand
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabile
2 CONT
2 CONT John I, Count of Alençon (d. 1191)
2 CONT
2 CONT Clemence (d. bef. 1189), married Juhel, Sire de Mayenne
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa (d. bef. 1149)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ela (d. 10 October 1174), married first William de Warenne, 3rd Earl of Surrey, and second Patrick of Salisbury, 1st Earl of Salisbury
2 CONT
2 CONT Helie died on 28 February 1141, in the Abbey de Perseigne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helie_of_Burgundy
