2 CONT
2 CONT Hélie de Bourgogne (c. 1080 – 28 February 1141) was the daughter of Eudes I and Sibylla de Bourgogne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1095, she married Bertrand de Toulouse, as his second wife. The two had one son:
2 CONT Pons (c.1098–1137).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrand succeeded his father as Comte de Toulouse in 1105, and in 1108, he set out for Outremer to claim his father's rights as Comte de Tripoli. Hélie accompanied him on this expedition, which resulted in the capture of Tripoli 
2 CONC in 1109; shortly after, their nephew, William-Jordan died of wounds, giving Bertrand an undisputed claim to Tripoli.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrand died in 1112, and Pons succeeded him in Tripoli. Hélie returned to France, where she married Guillaume (William) III de Ponthieu in 1115. They had twelve children, including two named Robert, two named Guillaume (William)
2 CONC , and two named Enguerrand:
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy II de Ponthieu (d. 1147)
2 CONT Guillaume (d. aft. 1166)
2 CONT Robert
2 CONT Robert de Garennes (d. aft. 1171), a monk
2 CONT Guillaume
2 CONT Enguerrand
2 CONT Enguerrand
2 CONT Mabile
2 CONT Jean I, Comte d"Alençon (d. 1191)
2 CONT Clemence (d. bef. 1189), married Juhel, Sire de Mayenne
2 CONT Philippa (d. bef. 1149)
2 CONT Ela (d. 10 October 1174), married first Guillaume de Warenne, 3rd Earl of Surrey, and second Patrick of Salisbury, 1st Earl of Salisbury
2 CONT
2 CONT Hélie died on 28 February 1141, in the Abbey de Perseigne.
