1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT She was born in Mecca c. 546, the daughter of Abdul Muttalib ibn Hashim and Fatimah bint Amr al-Makhzumiya. She was the twin sister of Abdullah, the father of Muhammad. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Umm Hakim was known as Al-Baydaa ("the White One") because she was Abdulmuttalib's only fair-skinned daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Kurayz ibn Rabia from the Abdshams clan of the Quraysh. Their children were Amir, Arwa (the mother of the future Caliph Uthman), Talha and Umm Talha.
2 CONT
2 CONT Umm Hakim died before 610.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Given name has also been reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ummu'l Hakim al-Bayda' binte Imaam 'Abd al-Muṭṭalib
2 CONT * '''Umm Hakim bint Abdul Muttalib Abdul Muttalib
