2 TITL The Thervingian Line
2 NOTE Sisebuto's wife, the mother of Teodora and Recaredo II, was the daughter of Recaredo I and Floresinda. Another thing: On this chart, Ervixio (Ervigio) is the father AND husband of Cixilona. In Geni, Cixilone married Egica I. Also,
3 CONC  what is the difference between "X", "G", and "KH"?
2 NOTE This chart is from Wikipedia.  I've done a lot of research myself and you are correct the leaders of the Visigoths were chosen and elected but the ones who are chosen were related in some way., like a brother-in-law, uncle, cousin
3 CONC , or a son of the last king.  (Example) l Alaric ! elected Ataulf t his brother-in-law who become the new leader of the Visigoths, then after  Ataulf the Visigoths elected the son-in-law of  Alaric 1, Theodoric II and so on.  Plea
3 CONC se consider  studying Project Medlands which is considered a main source of information about the Visigoths.   The Visigoths Line is a mess here on Geni.   
2 NOTE The chart is confusing using Greek/Armenian names for Visigoths, titling..of the Thervingian Line (old name long since gone out of use when Visigoth became the moniker and usually spelled Teurvingian or Tervingian. Chart also make
3 CONC s it look like Suintila and Teodora had five children, three of whom became kings even though they were born at or after the death of Suintila.  The visigothic throne was not necessarily inherited. Kings were chosen by Bishops and
3 CONC  Patricians and were often not connected with one another.
1 NOTE  Grego natural de Constantinopla, o qual, vindo para Espanha el-rei Chindasuindo, o casou com uma sobrinha sua, e tiveram o filho Ervígio.
2 CONT [Frei Manuel do Amor Divino Bessa (1762; 1997). ÁRVORE GENEALÓGICA DA ASCENDÊNCIA DE JOÃO PEREIRA DE ALMEIDA BEÇA DE VASCONCELOS e de seus irmãos da Quinta de Pinhete e de outras famílias que lhe pertencem. Prefácio, Notas, Adenda
2 CONC  e Índice Onomástico do Arqº Álvaro Magro de Moura Bessa. Porto: Livraria Civilização Editora.] 
1 NOTE There has been much controversy over the origin of Artabasto. Historians say, Greece and others say Armenia. Also known as Grego Balt
2 CONT In any case I found his wife Anna and her rich parentage, the history goes back a little further as a result.
2 CONT Was Governor, Strategegos, of the Armeniac Theme by Emeperor Anastasius II in 713. After the fall of Anastasius, Artavastos made a pact with Konon, Leon III, who was the governor of the Anatolic Theme. Together they overthrew Theo
2 CONC dosius III. The pact was cemented with the maryoragzo of Leo's daughter, Anna to Artavastos. The marriage took place after Leo III ascended the throne in March of 717. Artavasdos was given the Kouropalates, Master of the palace an
2 CONC d became the commander, Count, Komes of Opsikion Theme. His son was Nicephorus co emperor 742-743.
2 CONT War eventuall came and on Nov 2 743, Artavastos and his sons were publically blinded and exiled to the monastary at Chora.
2 CONT 1: Collins, Roger. Visigothic Spain, 409-711.
2 CONT Blackwell publishing 2004.
2 CONT 2: King, P.D., King Chindasuinth and the first territorial law code of the Visigothic kingdon.
2 CONT Edward James-Oxford-Clarendon Press 1980, PP. 131-157.
