1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===== Not  son of https://www.geni.com/people/Ximeno-Aznar-Infante/6000000047507293883 (attempted historical fallacy, read below)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT B.      FAMILY of PELAYO FRÓILAZ "el Diácono"
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20EARLY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#PelayoFroilazdied1037A 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT  Three brothers, parents not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.       '''  FRUELA Jiménez''' .  Conde.  He founded the monastery of San Pedro de Teberga.  
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Fruela's wife is not known.  Fruela & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         PELAYO Froílaz “el Diácono" (-after 4 Oct 1032).  Conde. -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         SANCHO Jiménez . 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         PIÑOLO Jiménez .
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Su padre, el '''conde Froila Jiménez''', era hijo del conde Jimeno Díaz –hijo de Diego Fernández– y de su esposa, Adosinda Gutiérrez,[1] hija, a su vez, del conde Gutierre Menéndez y de la condesa Ilduara Ériz,[2][3] hija del cond
2 CONC e [https://www.geni.com/people/Ero-Fern%C3%A1ndez-de-Lugo-conde-de-Lugo/6000000001412968233 Ero Fernández].[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelayo_Froilaz_el_Di%C3%A1cono
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== The Summary of the Historical Fallacy
2 CONT The title of '''Royal Infante''' (Prince) given to [https://www.geni.com/people/Pelayo-el-Di%C3%A1cono-Fr%C3%B3ilaz/6000000003749003238 Pelayo Froilaz "the Deacon"] is an '''historical fallacy''' and a '''pseudohistorical myth'''.
2 CONT It was manufactured during the 16th and 17th centuries by '''Baroque chroniclers and genealogists''' who worked for powerful aristocratic families like the House of Silva. These authors falsified lineage trees to boost the prestig
2 CONC e of their patrons, claiming Pelayo was a direct grandson of [https://www.geni.com/people/Fruela-II-Le%C3%B3n-Rey-de-Asturias-Le%C3%B3n-y-Galicia/6000000003589226433 King Fruela II of León].
2 CONT In reality, contemporary medieval documents prove he was a powerful local nobleman, count, and royal standard-bearer (alférez), but not a prince. The genealogists created this myth by confusing and '''transferring the royal status
2 CONC  of his wife''', Aldonza Ordóñez (who actually had royal blood), onto Pelayo himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
