2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raymond_Ier_des_Baux
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariage et enfants[modifier | modifier le code] Il se marie en 1116 avec Étiennette de Provence et de Gévaudan, morte après 1160, fille de Gilbert, vicomte de Gévaudan, de Millau et de Carlat, et de Gerberge d'Arles, comtesse héri
2 CONC tière de Provence. Elle lui donna plusieurs enfants:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Hugues II, mort en Sardaigne en 1179, qui lui succède comme seigneur des Baux,
2 CONT #Guillaume, qui en 1130 cède avec ses frères des droits de passage au monastère de Boscodon. En 1150, après la mort de son père, il se soumet au Comte de Provence, devient chevalier de l'Ordre de Saint-Jean de Jérusalem et meurt a
2 CONC u printemps du 1160,
2 CONT #Bertrand Ier, mort vers 1181, seigneur des Baux après son frère, marié à Thiburge II, comtesse héritière d'Orange,
2 CONT #Alasacie, citée en 1142 et mariée à Pierre de Lambesc,
2 CONT #Gilbert, cité en 1137, meurt en 1160,
2 CONT #peut-être Matelle, mariée successivement à Pierre II de Gabarret, vicomte de Béarn, puis à Pierre-Centulle III, comte de Bigorre ;
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provaixmar.htm#RaymondBauxdied1150
2 CONT
2 CONT '''RAYMOND de Baux''', son of GUILLAUME-HUGUES de Baux & his wife Vierne --- ([1075/85]-Barcelona 1150). Guillaume-Hugues donated property, previously owned by his father Hugues de Baux, to the church of Saint-Trophime d'Arles, wi
2 CONC th the consent of Vierne his wife and their sons Hugues and Raymond by charter dated 1091[873]. He participated in the First Crusade: "…Raimundus de Balcio, decanus de Poscheriis…" subscribed the charter dated 31 Jan 1105 under wh
2 CONC ich "Raymundus comes S. Aegidii" confirmed donations to the church of Arles in articulo mortis[874]. A charter dated May 1110 refers to earlier donations to Lérins by "Guillelmus Ugonis et uxor eius Vierna et filiis eius Raimundus
2 CONC " and the current donation by "Raimundi de Balcio et mater sua"[875]. Ramón Berenguer Conde de Barcelona and his wife Douce granted la seigneurie de Berre to Raymond de Baux by charter dated 1116[876]. A bull of Pope Calixtus II d
2 CONC ated 22 Jun 1121 threatened excommunication against "Raimundi de Bautio, Guilelmo de Sabrano, Elesiario de Castrias, Rainoni de Castlar et Guilelmo Rainoardi" if they didn't prevent Alphonse Comte de Toulouse from attacking the mo
2 CONC nastery of Saint-Gilles, a subsequent bull dated 22 Apr 1122 noting that "…Raimundum de Baltio, Guillemum de Sabrano, Elisiarium de Castriis, Guillelmum Rainoardi de Mezenees, vicecomites de Mezoaga, et Rainonem de Castlar" had be
2 CONC en excommunicated for the same offence[877]. Raymond de Baux and Hugues his son confirmed a donation of property to the Knights Hospitallers of St John by charter dated 29 Jun 1137, in the presence of Gilbert son of Raymond and Pi
2 CONC erre-Isnard de Baux[878]. He was a contender to succeed as Comte de Provence in 1145, presumably basing his claim through his wife. "Raimundus de Baltio" swore allegiance to Raymond Archbishop of Arles by charter dated [1147][879]
2 CONC . Raymond de Baux, husband of Etiennette, and his sons made peace with Ramón Berenguer II Conde de Barcelona in 1150, but died before returning to Provence, whereupon his wife and sons Hugues, Guillaume, Bertrand and Gilbert confi
2 CONC rmed the peace agreement[880]: a charter dated 17 Mar 1273 records a document dated 1150 which record the origins of a war between "Raymond de Baux, Etiennette et des fils contre le Comte" and the allegiance sworn by "Etiennette f
2 CONC ille de la comtesse Gerberge, Hugues, Guillaume, Bertrand et Gilbert ses fils" to "Raymond conte de Barcelone"[881].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before [1110/15]) ETIENNETTE de Gévaudan, daughter of GIRBERT Vicomte de Gévaudan et de Millau & his wife Gerberge Ctss de Provence (-after 1160). ... ... .... .... ... ... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT    Raymond & his wife had seven children:
2 CONT ------
