2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HUG [IV] de Empúries (-Apr 1230).  He succeeded his father as Comte de Empúries.  "Ugo…comes Impuriarum et uxor mea Maria" sold property to the abbot of Santa María de Amer by charter dated 17 Dec 1210, which names "Pon
2 CONC tio Ugone bona memoria patre meo"[1593].  “Ugo Impuriarum comes et Maria uxor mea” founded a lamp in the church of Santa Maria de Pederdell by charter dated 17 Jul 1217[1594].  “Ugo...Impuriarum comes” sold “decimam...ad barchas..
2 CONC .de portu de Chadachers usque ad gradum Salatam” to Santa Maria de Roses by charter dated 17 Oct 1228, signed by “Marie...Impuriarum comitissa eius uxoris...”[1595].  “Ugo...Impuriarum comes” reached agreement with Santa Maria de 
2 CONC Roses on matters of jurisdiction by charter dated 30 Jun 1229[1596].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MARÍA de Vilademuls Señora de Vilademuls, daughter of --- (-after 17 Oct 1228).  "Ugo…comes Impuriarum et uxor mea Maria" sold property to the abbot of Santa María de Amer by charter dated 17 Dec 1210, which names "Pontio 
2 CONC Ugone bona memoria patre meo"[1597].  The primary source which confirms her family origin has not yet been identified.  “Ugo Impuriarum comes et Maria uxor mea” founded a lamp in the church of Santa Maria de Pederdell by charter d
2 CONC ated 17 Jul 1217[1598].  “Ugo...Impuriarum comes” sold “decimam...ad barchas...de portu de Chadachers usque ad gradum Salatam” to Santa Maria de Roses by charter dated 17 Oct 1228, signed by “Marie...Impuriarum comitissa eius uxor
2 CONC is...”[1599].  Hug [IV] & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         PONCE [IV] de Empúries (-after 1269).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded his father as Comte de Empúries. -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         GUILLERMINA (-after 1277).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m BERENGUER de Cabrera, son of --- (-1248). 
