2 CONT
2 CONT 3.      '''   JUSIANA de Entenza''' (-after 1213).  Santiago names “Berenguer, Gombal y Jusiana” as the children of “Ponce Hugo” and his wife, adding that the two sons died without heirs, but does not cite the corresponding primar
2 CONC y source[2516].  Zurita records the marriage of “D. Bernaldo Guillen”, son of “Guillen de Mompeller...y...Doña Ynes”, and “Doña Iusiana, hija de Ponce Ugo hermano del Conde de Ampurias, que por parte de la madre era del linaje de 
2 CONC Entença”, arranged by Jaime I King of Aragon who granted him “gran Estado en su Reyno”[2517].  The passage is recorded in the paragraph dealing with events in 1213, but the reference to King Jaime (then an infant and only just suc
2 CONC ceeded to the throne) suggests that the marriage must have taken place later.  Señora de Alcolea.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([after 1213]) BERNARD GUILLAUME de Montpellier, son of GUILLAUME [VIII] Seigneur de Montpellier & his second [bigamous] wife Inés de Castilla ([1190/95]-1237).  Bernard Guillaume & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         BERNAT GUILLEM [I] de Entenza (-after 20 Aug 1296).  Zurita records that “Don Bernardo Guillen de Entença” claimed “la villa y señorio de Mompeller” in 1264 as heir of “Don Bernardo Guillen su padre, que murio en el Pu
2 CONC ch de S. Maria...”[2518].  -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         SIBILA de Entenza (-[after 1264]).  Zurita records that “Don Pedro Fernandez de Vergua, hijo de Don Fortuño de Vergua de Pueyo” had married “Doña Sibilia de Entença, prima del Rey, hija de Don Bernaldo Guillen”[2519]. 
2 CONC  m PEDRO Fernández de Vergua, son of FORTUN de Vergua de Pueyo & his wife --- (-after 1264). 
