1 OCCU Señora de Alcocer, Salmerón, Viana and Azañón, señora de Alcocer, Cifuentes, Viana de Mondéjar, Palazuelos, Salmerón y Valdeolivas
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mayor Guillén de Guzmán ( ?, 1205 - Alcocer ,1262 ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Born into one of the level two "richmen" families of King Ferdinand III's court, she was the daughter of Guillén Pérez de Guzmán, and sister of Pedro de Guzmán, Castile's first adelantado and father of Alonso Pérez de Guzmán.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was mentioned in chronicles and documents of the time mainly for being the lover of prince Alfonso de Castilla, future king Alfonso X of Castile, son of Ferdinand III of Castile and Beatriz de Suabia.
2 CONT
2 CONT From her relation with prince Alfonso she had three children[citation needed]:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Beatrice (1242 - 1303), married to Alfonso III of Portugal and mother of Denis I of Portugal;
2 CONT *Martín Alfonso de Castilla (? - ?), abbot in Valladolid
2 CONT * Urraca (? - ?).
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 4 October 1262. Her body was buried in the monastery of the Order of Poor Ladies of San Miguel del Monte. After moving to Alcocer, her body was moved as well, and it curiously remained intact until the beginning othe 2
2 CONC 1st century. In 1936, it disapeared together with a polycromated wooden statue, considered among he best funerary art from the Middle Ages in Guadalajara[citation needed].
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_Guillen_de_Guzm%C3%A1n
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Castile (1242-1303)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice of Castile was an illegitimate daughter of Alfonso X of Castile and Maria de Guzman.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SPANISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER%20MEDIEVAL.htm#GuillenPerezGuzmanMElviraRodriquez
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         GUILLÉN Pérez de Guzman (-after 30 Jun 1244) m (before May 1222) as her second husband, MARÍA González Girón, widow of GIL Vásquez de Soverosa, daughter of GONZALO Rodríguez Girón & his first wife Sancha Rodríguez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillen & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         MARÍA [Mayor] Guillén de Guzmán ([1225]-Alcocer before 1267, bur Alcocer, monastery of Santa Clara).  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Pedro Nuñez de Guzman, D. Maria Guillen de Guzman" as the childre
2 CONC n of "D. Guillen Perez de Guzman" and his wife "D. Elvira Rodriguez"[1244].  Señora de Alcocer, Salmerón, Viana and Azañón.  The Crónica del Rey Don Alfonso X names "doña Mayor Guillen…fija de don Pedro Guzman" as mother of King A
2 CONC lfonso X´s daughter "doña Beatriz, que fué casada con el rey don Alfonso de Portugal"[1245].  Mistress: ([1243/48]) of Infante don ALFONSO de Castilla y León, son of FERNANDO III "el Santo" King of Castile and León & his first wif
2 CONC e Elisabeth von Hohenstaufen (Toledo 23 Nov 1221-Seville 4 Apr 1284, bur Seville, Cathedral Santa María).  He succeeded his father in 1252 as ALFONSO X "el Sabio" King of Castile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CASTILE.htm#AlfonsoXdied1284B
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (3): ([1243/48]) MARÍA [Mayor] Guillén de Guzmán, Señora de Alcocer, Salmerón, Viana and Azañón, daughter of GUILLÉN Pérez de Guzmán Señor de Vecilla & his wife María González Girón ([1225]-Alcocer before 1267, bur Alcoce
2 CONC r, monastery of Santa Clara).  The Crónica del Rey Don Alfonso X names "doña Mayor Guillen…fija de don Pedro Guzman" as mother of King Alfonso X´s daughter "doña Beatriz, que fué casada con el rey don Alfonso de Portugal"[1086]. 
