1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Geoffroy IV Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine,''' or Geoffrey 'the Fair' d'Anjou, was born on 24 August 1113. He was the son of '''Fulk V d'Anjou, 9th Comte d'Anjou and Aremburga de la Fleche, Comtesse de Main
2 CONC e'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married '''Matilda 'the Empress' of England''', daughter of Henry I 'Beauclerc', King of England and Editha of Scotland, on 22 May 1128 at Le Mans Cathedral, Le Mans, France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey's and Matilda's children were:
2 CONT * '''Henry II of England''' (1133–1189)
2 CONT * '''Geoffrey, Count of Nantes''' (1 June 1134 Rouen- 26 July 1158 Nantes) died unmarried and was buried in Nantes
2 CONT * '''William X, Count of Poitou''' (1136–1164) died unmarried
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey also had illegitimate children by an unknown mistress (or mistresses): '''Hamelin; Emme''', who married Dafydd Ab Owain Gwynedd, Prince of North Wales; and '''Mary''', who became a nun and Abbess of Shaftesbury and who ma
2 CONC y be the poetess Marie de France. '''Adelaide of Angers''' is sometimes sourced as being the mother of Hamelin.www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8143822/geoffrey-plantagenet_iv
