2 CONT He died on 7 September 1151 at age 38 at Château-du-Loir, France. He was buried at Le Mans Cathedral, Le Mans, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the title of 10th Comte d'Anjou in 1129. He succeeded to the title of 12th Duc de Normandie on 19 January 1144. He gained the title of Comte de Maine.  He abdicated as Duke of Normandy in 1150.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT a conflict of death date with a duplicate profile: 15 Jan
2 CONT
2 CONT and burial location:
2 CONT
2 CONT Labbey dessergela, Angers
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT "Geoffrey V (24 August 1113 – 7 September 1151), called the Handsome (French: le Bel) and Plantagenet, was the Count of Anjou, Touraine, and Maine by inheritance from 1129 and then Duke of Normandy by conquest from 1144. By his ma
2 CONC rriage to the Empress Matilda, daughter and heiress of Henry I of England, Geoffrey had a son, Henry Curtmantle, who succeeded to the English throne and founded the Plantagenet dynasty to which Geoffrey gave his nickname."
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================================
