2 CONC nd is one reason he could not intervene in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 7 September 1151, Geoffrey died suddenly. According to John of Marmoutier, Geoffrey was returning from a royal council when he came down with a fever. He arrived at Château-du-Loir, collapsed on a couch, made bequests of gifts 
2 CONC and charities, and died. He was buried at St. Julien's Cathedral in Le Mans France.
2 CONT --------------------
