2 TITL Geoffrey V Plantagenet
2 NOTE Geoffrey Plantagenet "Le Bon", V Comte d'Anjou is your 19th great grandfather.
2 NOTE Geoffrey Plantagenet "Le Bon", V Comte d'Anjou is your 22nd great grandfather. 
2 NOTE Geoffrey Plantagenet, Count of Anjou is your 21st great grandfather.
2 NOTE Notes for GEOFFREY V Plantagenet 10th Count of Anjou:
3 CONT
3 CONT He was the Count of Anjou & Duke of Normandy. Family acquired the surname "Plantagenet" from the nickname given Geoffrey because he wore as a badge a sprig of flowering Broom (Plants genista), a habit said to have originated when 
3 CONC retrieving his hat, which fell off one day while hunting, he scooped up a handful of yellow broom flowers. The name was not formally used until the mid 15th century, when Richard, Duke of York, claimed the throne through superior 
3 CONC right and called himself Richard Plantagenet to emphasize his claim. Was only 14 when his father married him off to Matilda-heir apparent to the English throne.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Geoffrey in his profile.
