1 NOTE  Nicknamed "Le Bon" (The Handsome), Count of Anjou and Maine. The origin of the Plantagenet surname is somewhat nebulous. A plume of yellow broom-straw (Planta-genistae) was worn in the helm of Geoffrey's armor. Some say that it's
2 CONC  origin came when his father, Fulk the Great made a pilgrimage to Jerusalem and was scourged for his sins with broom twigs. Whatever the origin, the surname "Plantagenet" was used by his son, Henry II and subsequent Kings of Engla
2 CONC nd.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-7369
