1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LETAUD, son of HUGUES du Perche & his wife Beatrix de Mâcon (-after [1050]).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 26 May 1028 under which Francon Bishop of Paris agreed with "Albericum illius supradicti
2 CONC  Gosfredi filium et heredum", concerning a prior grant by the bishop's predecessor to "Gosfrido comiti Landonensi castri", with the approval of "fratribus ipsius Alberici, filiis Hugonis Pertice…Gosfredo et Letoldo"[301].  "…Letal
2 CONC di militis…" witnessed a charter dated [1050] under which Bishop Isembard restored the customs of Beaulay to the abbey of Saint-Euverte d’Orléans[302], although it is possible that this signature relates to Létaud [II] see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ---.  The name of Létaud's wife is not known. 
2 CONT
