1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Erard I of Brienne
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Erard I, Count of Brienne (c. 1090 – c. 1120?) was Count of Brienne at the end of the 10th century. He was the son of Gautier I of Brienne, count of Brienne, and his wife Eustachie of Tonnerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1097 he fought in the First Crusade.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1110 he married Alix of Roucy-Ramerupt, daughter of André de Montdidier-Roucy, seigneur de Ramerupt. They had 3 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT Gautier II of Brienne, count of Brienne and lord of Ramerupt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy of Brienne
2 CONT
2 CONT Félicité of Brienne, who married Simon I of Broyes then in 1142 Geoffroy III, sire de Joinville.
