1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wulgrin III of Angoulême
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wulgrin_III_of_Angoul%C3%AAme
2 CONT
2 CONT Wulgrim III of Angoulême, inherited the territory of Count of Angoulême from his father, William IV of Angoulême.
2 CONT
2 CONT His untimely death, was the first break in the house of Wulgrim which had ruled Angoulême since the days of the Carolingians. As he had only one daughter, Mathilde of Angoulême, the territory went to his younger brother, William V
2 CONC  of Angoulême. His daughter Mathilde would marry Hugh IX of Lusignan, who would eventually inherit the kingdom, over the claims of John of England, through Isabella of Angoulême, the daughter of Aymer of Angoulême, the third and y
2 CONC oungest brother.
