2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hugh VIII of Lusignan From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were: Hugues de Lusignan, Co-Seigneur de Lusignan in 1164 (c. 1141 - 1169), married before 1162 Orengarde N, who died in 1169, leaving an infant son Hugues who was to become Hugh IX of Lusignan, and an infant son Raou
2 CONC l who was to become Raoul I de Lusignan
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh IX the Brown of Lusignan (1163 or 1168 – 5 November 1219)[1] was the grandson of Hugh VIII. His father, also Hugh (b. c. 1141), was the co-seigneur of Lusignan from 1164, marrying a woman named Orengarde before 1162 or about 
2 CONC 1167 and dying in 1169.www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh VIII de Lusignan
2 CONT BIRTH	1141
2 CONT Lusignan, Departement de la Vienne, Poitou-Charentes, France
2 CONT DEATH	11 Apr 1169 (aged 27–28)
2 CONT Jordan
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Abbaye Notre-Dame de Valence
2 CONT Couhe, Departement de la Vienne, Poitou-Charentes, France 
2 CONT PLOT	Crusader graves, no marker
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	111140412
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Lusignan. Husband of Orengarde Bourgogne de Rancon. This Hugh died while on Crusade in Palestine. His heart was returned for burial at Valence. Date of burial noted as 15 March 1169. His parents were Hugh (1120-1173) and Rour
2 CONC gogne (Dame de Fontenay). He was the grandson of Hugh and wife Sarazine of Armenia.
2 CONT Only a part of the dining hall of the monks remains of this abbey.
2 CONT
