1 NOTE Gui de Lusignan came to rule Jerusalem from his brother-in-law Baldwin IV in 1186 to 1194.  He and his Queen, Sibyella, were deposed by Saladin in  1192.   He then went to Cyrus and ruled until 1194.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gui de Lusignan, who had been King of Jerusalem, sided with  his cousin, King Richard I of England against Saladin, in return Richard granted Guy de Lusignan the throne of Cyprus which he ruled from 1192 to 1194.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Henry II banished Guy or Gui de Lusignan from England for murder. Gui de Lusignan was a first cousin of King Henry's wife Eleanor of Aquitaine.
1 NOTE He was Count of Jaffa and Ascalon in 1180. He was crowned in 1186. He resigned in 1192. He became King of Cyprus in 1192.
