1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William VII of Montpellier was the eldest son of William VI and of his wife Sibylle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aged around 15, he inherited the lordship of Montpellier from his father in 1146 under the tutelage of his grandmother, Ermessende of Melgueil. In 1156 he married Matilda of Burgundy, daughter of Hugh II, Duke of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fell ill in 1171 and made his will on St Michael's day (29 September 1171), appointing his brother Gui Guerrejat and John of Montlaur, bishop of Maguelonne, as joint guardians of his young sons. He probably died in 1172.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Matilda had nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibylle, who married Rayomond Gaucelm of Lunel 
2 CONT
2 CONT William VIII of Montpellier 
2 CONT
2 CONT another William, who died between 1171 and 1180 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gui, named Gui Burgundion after his mother and to distinguish him from his uncle Gui Guerrejat. He married Azalais of Conas and had a daughter, Burgundione 
2 CONT
2 CONT Raymond, who became a Cistercian monk at Grandselve, then bishop of Lodève, then (by 1192) bishop of Agde 
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillemette, who married Raymond of Anduze, son of Bernard V of Anduze 
2 CONT
2 CONT Azalais or Adelaide 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie 
2 CONT
2 CONT Clémence, who was for some time a nun, but in 1199 married Rostaing of Sabran, constable of the count of Toulouse
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
