1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Eleonore Dss d’Aquitaine, Ctss de Poitou, Ctss de Saintonge, Angoûmois, Limousin, Auvergne, Bordeaux et Agen, Queen Consort of England
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/William-X-Duke-of-Aquitaine/6000000003523986134?through=6000000003582502504 GUILLAUME d'Aquitaine] (1099-Santiago de Compostela 9 Apr 1137, bur Santiago de Compostela)
2 CONT x [https://www.geni.com/people/Eleanor-of-Ch%C3%A2tellerault-Duchess-of-Aquitaine/6000000000701127473?through=6000000003582502504 ELEONORE de Châtellerault], d/o AMAURY [I] Vicomte de Châtellerault & his wife Amauberge "Dangerose"
2 CONC [601] --- (-after Mar 1130)
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''[https://www.geni.com/people/Eleonore-d-Aquitaine/6000000003582502504 ELEONORE d'Aquitaine] (Nieul-sur-Autize, Vendée or Château de Belin, Guyenne or Palais d’Ombrière, Bordeaux 1122-Abbaye de Fontevrault 1 Apr 1204, bur Abbay
2 CONC e de Fontevrault).''' 
2 CONT >The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Alienor Guilielmi filia comits Pictavorum et Aquitanie ducis" as wife of "regi Francie Ludovico"[606].  “Willelmus…dux Aquitanorum” donated property to “ecclesiæ B. Hilarii de Ce
2 CONC lla” (La Celle, outside Poitiers) granted by “Gaufredus avus et Guillelmus pater mei” by charter dated 3 Mar 1130, subscribed by “Willielmi ducis Aquitanorum, Aenordis comitissæ, Alienordis filiæ eorum, Wilelmi Aigres filii eorum”
2 CONC [607].  She succeeded her father in 1137 as ELEONORE Dss d’Aquitaine, Ctss de Poitou, Ctss de Saintonge, Angoûmois, Limousin, Auvergne, Bordeaux et Agen.  She left France with her husband in Jun 1147 on the Second Crusade[608].  "
2 CONC Helienordis...Francorum regina et Aquitanorum ducissa" confirmed the privileges of Notre-Dame de Saintes, at the request of "Agnetis abbatisse", with the consent of “Ludovici regis Francorum et ducis Aquitanorum collateralis nostr
2 CONC i et Aelith sororis nostre”, by charter dated 1151[609].  She was crowned Queen Consort of England with her husband 19 Dec 1154 at Westminster Abbey.  She supported the revolt of her sons against their father in 1173, was captured
2 CONC  and imprisoned in the château de Chinon, later at Salisbury until 1179.  The Continuator of Florence of Worcester records the death "XII Kal Apr" [1204] of "regina Alienor" and her burial "ad Fontem Ebraldi"[610].  The Chronicle 
2 CONC of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records the burial of "uxor [regis Henrici] regina Alienordis" in the same abbey as her husband[611]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
