1 NOTE Primo y yerno del Rey Alfonso VIII "El de las Navas", hijo del Rey Fernando II de León y padre del Rey Fernando III, unificador de Castilla y León. Subió al trono en 1188. Conquistó Mérida a los musulmanes.-
1 NOTE Founded the university of Palencia in 1209-the first of the Spanish universities.
2 CONT He endowed the royal abbey of Las Huelgas, near Burgos, in 1187, at his wife's request; the abbey was also to be their royal mausoleum.  In 1195 Alfonso was defeated by the Moors at Alarcos, and Castile was invaded by the armies o
2 CONC f neighboring Leon and Navarre, but he fought back and forced their leaders to terms.  In 1212 he led Leon and Navarre to a great victory over the Moors at Las Navas de Tolosa. [Cope.FTW]
