2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         JOFRE [II] de Rocabertí (-killed in battle 1212).  Vescomte de Rocabertí.  m (after 1202) ADELAIS [Ermesinde] de Montpellier, daughter of GUILLAUME [VII] Seigneur de Montpellier & his second [bigamous] wife Agnes ---.  
2 CONC In his testament dated 4 Nov 1202, her father bequeathed money to "filiabus meis Agneti et Adalaiz"[1646].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not been identified.  Jofre [II] & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         DALMAU [II] de Rocaberti (-1229).  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names “Dalmau V †1229 vescomte de Rocaberti (baró de Vilademuls?)” as son of Jofre [II].  The primary s
2 CONC ource which confirms this information have not been identified.  Vescomte de Rocabertí.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ARSENDA de Pinos [or Bonet?], daughter of ---.  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names “Arsenda de Pinos (o Bonet?)” as wife of Dalmau [V].  The primary source which confirms this 
2 CONC information have not been identified.  Dalmau [II] & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''i)          HUG JOFRE [I] de Rocabertí (-1250).  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names “Hug Jofre I †1250 vescomte de Rocaberti (baró de Vilademuls?)” as son of Dalmau.  The prim
2 CONC ary source which confirms this information have not been identified.  Vescomte de Rocabertí.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m MARÍA de Aragon, [illegitimate daughter of PEDRO II "el Católico" King of Aragon & his mistress ---].  The genealogical table of the Rocaberti family in the Gran Enciclopèdia Catalana names “(Maria de Aragó?)” as wife of Hug Jof
2 CONC re [I].  The primary source which confirms this information have not been identified.  If she was the daughter of Pedro II, she was born before 1213, which from a chronological point of view seems unlikely considering the marriage
2 CONC  date of Hug Jofre [I]’s paternal grandparents shown above.''' 
