2 TITL Louis Vll "The Younger" King of France
2 NOTE Louis VII, called the Younger or the Young (French: Louis le Jeune; 1120 – 18 September 1180), was King of France, the son and successor of Louis VI (hence his nickname). He ruled from 1137 until his death. He was a member of the 
3 CONC House of Capet. His reign was dominated by feudal struggles (in particular with the Angevin family), and saw the beginning of the long feud between France and England. It also saw the beginning of construction on Notre-Dame de Par
3 CONC is and the disastrous Second Crusade.
3 CONT Read more about Louis VII in his profile.
