1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marguerite de France (1158-1197)
2 CONT
2 CONT Un article de Wikipédia, l'encyclopédie libre.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_de_France_(1158-1197)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite de France, née en 1158, morte à Acre en 1197, fille de Louis VII, roi de France, et de Constance de Castille.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle épouse en premières noces le 21 août 1172 Henri le Jeune (1155-1183), fils du roi Henri II d'Angleterre et d'Aliénor d'Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT Veuve, elle se remarie en 1186 Béla III (1148 † 1196), roi de Hongrie. Celui-ci s'engage dans la croisade et ils meurent tous les deux en Terre Sainte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle n'eut pas d'enfants de ses deux mariages.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of France (November 1157 – August/September 1197) was the eldest daughter of Louis VII of France by his second wife Constance of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Early life 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 First marriage 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Second marriage 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Later life 
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite was a younger half-sister to Marie de Champagne and Alix of France. She was an older sister to Alys, Countess of the Vexin. Constance died in giving birth to Alys on 4 October 1160. Marguerite and Alys were older half-s
2 CONC isters to Philip II of France and Agnes of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maternal grandparents were Alfonso VII of Castile and Berenguela of Barcelona. Berenguela was a daughter of Ramon Berenguer III, Count of Barcelona by his third wife Douce of Provence.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was betrothed to Henry the Young King of England on 2 November 1160. Henry was the second of five sons born to Henry II of England and Eleanor of Aquitaine. He was five years old at the time of this agreement while Marguerite 
2 CONC was only two.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] First marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband became co-ruler with his father in 1170. They were formally married on 27 August 1172 in Winchester Cathedral. Marguerite became pregnant and gave birth to their only son William on 19 June 1177. The child was born pre
2 CONC maturely and died on 22 June of the same year. She was accused in 1182 of having a love affair with William Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke, although contemporary chroniclers doubted the truth of these accusations. Henry may have st
2 CONC arted the process to have their marriage annulled, ostensibly due to her adultery but in reality because she could not conceive an heir. Marguerite was sent back to France, according to E. Hallam (The Plantagenets) and Amy Kelly (
2 CONC Eleonore of Aquitaine and the Four Kings), to ensure her safety during the civil war with Young Henry's brother Richard. Her husband died in 1183 while on campaign in the Dordogne region of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Second marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT After receiving a substantial pension in exchange for surrendering her dowry of Gisors and the Vexin, she became the second Queen consort of Béla III of Hungary in 1186. The difficult delivery of her only known child in 1177 seems
2 CONC  to have rendered her sterile, as she had no further children by either Young Henry or Béla.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Later life
2 CONT
2 CONT She was widowed for a second time in 1196 and died on pilgimage to the Holy Land at St John of Acre in 1197, having only arrived a few days prior to her death. She was buried at the Cathedral of Tyre, according to Ernoul the chron
2 CONC icler who continued the chronicles of William of Tyre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal titles 
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT
