1 CONT In-Reply-To: B.C.Tompsett@computer-science.hull.ac.uk (Brian Tompsett) "Re: Arab Royalty > Spain > England" (Jan 3, 11:57am)
1 CONT References: <9501031157.AA25104@olympus.dcs.hull.ac.uk>
1 CONT X-Mailer: Z-Mail (3.0.0 15dec93)
1 CONT To: B.C.Tompsett@uk.ac.hull.computer-science (Brian Tompsett)
1 CONT Subject: Re: Arab Royalty > Spain > England
1 CONT Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
1 CONT Mime-Version: 1.0
1 CONT Sender: rikv@COM.MENTORG.wv
1 CONT Status: RO
1 CONT
1 CONT Brian, I know what you mean about cross-link documentation.  Wish I could get
1 CONT some more & I suspect it's out there.
1 CONT
1 CONT I have had suggested to me the following:
1 CONT
1 CONT -- Mohammed
1 CONT -- Rukaiya m. Caliph Uthman/Otman ben Affan
1 CONT -- Aisha bint (d/o) Otman m. Merwan ben Hakim
1 CONT -- ?? bint Merwan m. Muza ben Nuseir el-Bekra (660-718)
1 CONT -- Abd-al-Aziz ibn Musa (d. 717) m. ??
1 CONT    There also is a claim that this fellow is a son, not grandson of
1 CONT    Merwan ben Hakim.  (This is true in all charts I've seen -- RikV)
1 CONT -- Aisha (?) m. Fortun Benqasim
1 CONT -- Muza ben Fortun m. ??
1 CONT -- Muza ben Muza m. ??
1 CONT -- Oria Benqasi m. Fortun Garces le Borgne, King of Pamplona
1 CONT    (son of Garcia Iniguez)
1 CONT -- Oneca Fortunez of Pamplona m. Aznar Sanchez of Larron
1 CONT -- Toda m. Sancho I (865-925), King of Navarre
1 CONT -- Garcia III (919-970), King of Navarre m. Andregoto, Cdsa de Aragon
1 CONT -- Sancho II (935-994), King of Navarre m. Urraca, dau. of Cdr Fernando of
1 CONT    Castile
1 CONT -- Garcia IV (964-999), King of Navarre m. Jimena Vermudez
1 CONT -- Sancho III (990-1035), King of Navarre m. Munia, dau. of Sancho I of Leon
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Two things you could check on for me, since I can't find my notes on Fortun &
1 CONT family: Do you have any reference to Fortun's wife?  He was actually a Basque
1 CONT convert, but went to Damascus.  Apparently (according to this data) he must
1 CONT have married there.  His family (Banu) was Qasi, hence Banuqasi.  I also show
1 CONT that Musa Ibn Musa (Musa son of Musa) married his step sister Assona Iniguez,
1 CONT daughter of Jimeno of Pamplona.  Jimeno married Musa Ibn Fortun's widow (not
1 CONT named) and from this marriage come the early kings of Pamplona/Navarre. Any
1 CONT references you have on Fortun and the two Musa's
1 CONT
1 CONT Second:  Mohammed the Prophet had a daughter Rukaiyya, and her marriage to
1 CONT Othman is known, but are there documented descendants?
1 CONT
1 CONT We may need to start a special interest group!
1 CONT
1 CONT blauensteiner@edvz.tuwien.ac.at (Albert Blauensteiner, Vienna)
1 CONT camfield@olympus.net (Tom Camfield, Port Townsend, Washington, USA)
1 CONT
1 CONT Tom also has a correspondent in Norway; also one of the guys who responded
1 CONT to the original Arab post, but I guess he's pretty busy on his doctorate.
1 CONT
1 CONT Rik.
1 CONT
