0 @N6000000000945071318@ NOTE Nuña (eller Major) var arving til Castilla. 
1 CONT Rikets infanter beskylte henne for ekteskapsbrudd. Cortés ble sammenkalt og bestemte
1 CONT at hun skulle forsvare seg ved duell. Ramiro I, Sanchos eldste sønn, erklærte seg beredt til å
1 CONT kjempe for dronningens ære, hvoretter bakvaskerne tok beskyldningen tilbake og hennes ære
1 CONT var reddet.
1 CONT Hun hadde tre sønner, Garcia, Fernando og Gonzalo.
0 @N6000000002187750456@ NOTE Mayor of Castile
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Mayor of Castile (d. 1032) was queen of Navarre. She was originally called Muniadona (or Muñadona) and is variously called Munia (or Muña) Mayor (or just Munia or Muña). In Spanish, she is called Muniadona de Castilla. It is said 
1 CONC that her husband Sancho III of Navarre (Sancho the Great) renamed her from her contemporary name Muniadona to Mayor, for she was the eldest in her family, yet since she had an aunt of the same name, the story is clearly apocryphal
1 CONC . She was the daughter of Count Sancho I of Castile. Her marriage to Sancho made her Queen consort of Navarre.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1029, the Count García II of Castile, Mayor's brother, was assassinated by the Vela family, Castilian exiles in León. Mayor's husband, Sancho the Great, claimed his role as feudal overlord to pass the county to their second son
1 CONC , Ferdinand. Likewise this brought a nominal legitimate claim to the counties of Ribagorza and Sobrarbe to her husband, who has already taken control of them militarily.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mayor was the mother of four sons and at least one daughter:
1 CONT
1 CONT King Garcia V of Navarre 
1 CONT Ferdinand the Great, king of León and Castile 
1 CONT Gonzalo of Sobrarbe and Ribagorza 
1 CONT Bernardo 
1 CONT Jimena, wife of Bermudo III of León 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible, Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families Vol. 3 (chart 2186) by Michel L. Call ISBN 1-933194-22-7
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Gaia de Gascony Queen consort of Navarre
1 CONT 1010 – 1032 Succeeded by
1 CONT Estefanía de Foix 
0 @N6000000000945071458@ NOTE Bermudo ?den Verkbrudne? var konge av Leon 982 -   999. 
1 CONT Han kjempet mot sin fetter, Ramiro III og forenet Leon med Galicien og Castilla.
1 CONT I 992 ble han overvunnet av maurerne som hadde oversvømmet hans rike etter ordre
1 CONT av Almanzor. Han tilbrakte de siste år av sin regjeringstid med å reparere ruinene etter denne
1 CONT invasjon.
1 CONT Han var gift
1 CONT 1. gang i 983 med Velasquita av Castilla,
1 CONT 2. gang ca. 992 med hennes søster, Elvira.
