0 @N6000000002187755435@ NOTE Gonzalo of Sobrarbe and Ribagorza
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gonzalo Sánchez (assassinated 26 June 1043)[1] was made Count of Sobrarbe and Ribagorza, two small Pyrenean counties, before 1035 by his father, Sancho III of Navarre. He succeeded to these domains after his father's death in that
1 CONC  year and ruled them as vassal of his brother García until his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT He is thought to have been ineffectual and unpopular, with vassals defecting to his brother Ramiro during his own life, and one failing to name him in a list of rulers of Ribagorza written within a decade of his death. A late sour
1 CONC ce reports his assassination by one of his own knights, Ramonat de Uasconya, near Lascorz, and he was interred at San Victorián.[2] On his death, García awarded his counties to Ramiro, which initiated several centuries of Aragones
1 CONC e expansionism.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT Zurita, Gerónimo. Anales de la Corona de Aragón I. Edited by Antonio Ubieto Arteta and Desamparados Pérez Soler. Valencia: 1967. 
1 CONT Nelson, Lynn. The Aragonese Acquisition of Sobrarbe and Ribagorza. Estudios en Homenaje a Don Claudio Sánchez Albornoz en sus 90 Años, 2:227-236 (1982). 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Notes
1 CONT ^ His death on 26 June appears in the Necrology of San Victorián, but the year has been subject to much debate. Zurita places it in 1035, Moret in 1042 or 1043, Pérez de Urbel 1039 and Ubieto Arteta in in 1046. Nelson gives reason
1 CONC  to believe that it was 1043. Nelson, pp. 230-231. 
1 CONT ^ Nelson, pp. 228-229. 
0 @N6000000000945059405@ NOTE Regent av Leon 1027 - 1037. 
1 CONT Elvira ble oppdratt sammen med kong Alfons V.
1 CONT Hun deltok i sin dronningtid i katedralen sammen med Alfons V, biskopene og rikets
1 CONT herrer i det konsil som i 1020 vedtok det kjente ?Fueros de Leon?. Med Alfons fikk hun
1 CONT Bermudo III, Sancha og Jimena som ble mor til Cid Campeador.
0 @N6000000000437119886@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Galicia
0 @N6000000000437119842@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Princess Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Leon
0 @N6000000002187750864@ NOTE Sancha of León
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancha of León (1013 in Leon, Spain-1067 in Leon, Spain) was a daughter of Alfonso V of Leon by Elvira Mendes and Queen consort of Castile. She married Ferdinand I of León in 1032. She was a devout Catholic.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT She had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Sancho II of Castile (1040s - 1067). First son. 
1 CONT Alfonso VI of Castile (1040s - July 1, 1109). Second son. 
1 CONT García II of Galicia and Portugal (1040s - 1090s). Third son. 
1 CONT Elvira of Toro. Ruler of the city Toro. 
1 CONT Urraca of Zamora, Infanta of Castile. 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible, Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families Vol. 3 (chart 2186) by Michel L. Call ISBN 1-933194-22-7 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT New Creation Queen Consort of Castile
1 CONT 1037-1065 Succeeded by
1 CONT
1 CONT Alberta (Consort of Sancho II) 1071-1072
1 CONT Agnes of Aquitaine 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Jimena of Castile Queen Consort of León
1 CONT 1037-1065 Succeeded by
1 CONT Agnes of Aquitaine 
