0 @N6000000001783262036@ NOTE Raymond Borrel (in Catalan, Ramon Borrell and Spanish, Ramón Borrell) (972-1017) , was count of Barcelona, Girona, and Ausona from 992. Son of Borrell II of Barcelona and Letgarda de Rouergue. He was associated with his father fro
1 CONC m 988.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 993 he married Ermesinde de Carcassonne with whom he had one son: Berengar Raymond (c.1006).
1 CONT
1 CONT Between 1000 and 1002 he had to deal with a number of incursions by Al-Mansur. However Al-Mansur was killed in Battle of Calatañazor by Navarran and Leon forces. Seeing an opportunity Raymond counter-attacked in 1003 leading an ex
1 CONC pedition to Lleida. However this prompted a new raid on the County of Barcelona by Al-Mansur's son, Abd al-Malik.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1010, with the Cordoban Caliphate crumbling into civil war Raymond saw another opportunity. He organised a campaign against the Caliphate, with Armengol I of Urgell, Bernard of Besalú, and joined forces with Muhammad II of Córd
1 CONC oba. The army destroyed the forces of Caliph Suleiman II and sacked Cordoba. As a result Catalonia remained free from further Moorish dominion. Armengol died in battle on September 1 at Córdoba.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1015 and 1016 Raymond made further expeditions to the Rivers Ebro and Segre. The treasure obtained in these campaigns maintained the loyalty of his barons.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the County of Barcelona he ensured the repopulation of the Segarra, Conca de Barberà and Camp de Tarragona. He began the construction of the cathedral in Barcelona. He was also the first Catalan ruler to mint his own coinage.
1 CONT
1 CONT At his death in 1017, he was succeeded by his son Berengar Raymond under the regency of his mother. (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramon_Borrell,_Count_of_Barcelona)
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage: 20 Jan 0992 (http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/charts/of-barcelona-de-carcassonne.htm)
