1 CONT "Ramon Berenguer II, known as Cap d'Estopa, "towhead," from thethickness and colour of his hair. ...
1 CONT
1 CONT These twin sons were in power at Barcelona at the time of the Cid'sarrival. They do not appear to have accepted the Cid's estimate of hispersonal reputation and capacity; the exile was affronted by the lackof consideration which h
1 CONC e received and opened negotiations with theMoorish ruler of Zaragoza, Moctádir Ben Hud, who had been upon thethrone since 1046"
