0 @N6000000002187911595@ NOTE Hugh V of Lusignan
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh V (d.1060), called the Pious, was the fifth lord of Lusignan. He succeeded his father, Hugh IV, sometime around 1026.
1 CONT
1 CONT He and his brother Rorgo confirmed charters for the abbeys of Saint-Maixent and Saint-Cyprien and that of Nouaillé. He married Almodis, daughter of Bernard I, Count of La Marche, through which future counts would claim La Marche. 
1 CONC Almodis bore Hugh two sons: Hugh and Jordan. He then repudiated her on the basis of consanguinity and she married Pons of Toulouse. When Duke William VIII of Aquitaine, Hugh's suzerain, was at war with William IV of Toulouse, Almo
1 CONC dis persuaded Hugh to join her son's side. The duke besieged Lusignan and when Hugh tried to sortie for provisions, he was slain at the gate. He was succeeded by his eldest son, also named Hugh.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Hugh IV Lord of Lusignan Succeeded by:
1 CONT Hugh VI
