0 @N6000000001744806729@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Fulk "Rechin," Count of Anjou and chronicler. Having inherited the right to Touraine and Chateau-Landon, half of the Angevin inheritance, from his uncle Geoffrey Martel I, Fulk went to war against his brother Geoffrey, captured an
1 CONC d imprisoed him in 1066 and took Anjou and Saintonge into his domains. "The Chronicles of the Counts of Anjou" tells that his wife eloped with Philip I of France in 1107. Fulk himself was the initiator of these chronicles of his f
1 CONC orebears in the 1090s.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: Elizabeth Hallam, The Plantagenet Encyclopedia (NY: Crescent Books, 1996) 81.
1 CONT
1 CONT [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 2, Ed. 1, Tree #1241, Date of Import: May 8, 1997]
1 CONT
1 CONT !COUNT OF ANJOUFulk "Rechin," Count of Anjou and chronicler. Having inherited the right to Touraine and Chateau-Landon, half of the Angevin inheritance, from his uncle Geoffrey Martel I, Fulk went to war against his brother Geoffr
1 CONC ey, captured and imprisoed him in 1066 and took Anjou and Saintonge into his domains. "The Chronicles of the Counts of Anjou" tells that his wife eloped with Philip I of France in 1107. Fulk himself was the initiator of these chro
1 CONC nicles of his forebears in the 1090s.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: Elizabeth Hallam, The Plantagenet Encyclopedia (NY: Crescent Books, 1996) 81.
1 CONT
1 CONT [Brøderbund WFT Vol. 2, Ed. 1, Tree #1241, Date of Import: May 8, 1997]
