0 @N6000000002187911525@ NOTE Hugh VII of Lusignan
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh VII of Lusignan, called "le brun" (The Brown) (1065–1151) was the son of Hugh VI of Lusignan. He was one of the many notable Crusaders in the Lusignan family. In 1147 he took the Cross and followed King Louis VII of France on
1 CONC  the Second Crusade.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh married Sarrasine de Lezay (born 1067, died 1144). Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Hugh VIII of Lusignan
1 CONT    2. William de Lusignan, lord of Angles
1 CONT    3. Rorgon de Lusignan
1 CONT    4. Simon de Lusignan, lord of Lezay
1 CONT    5. Galeran de Lusignan
1 CONT    6. Ænor de Lusignan, married Geoffrey V de Thouars
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Hugh VI Count of La Marche
1 CONT 1110–1151 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Hugh VIII
