0 @N6000000004533040257@ NOTE Philippa (Matilda or Maud) of Toulouse, b. ca. 1073, divorced 1115/6,d. 28 Nov 1117; m. (1) Sancho Ramiros, King of Aragon; m. (2) 1094,William VII of Poitou (IX of Aquitaine), Count of Poitou, Duke ofAquitaine, b. ca. 22 Oct 1071
1 CONC , d. 10 Feb 1126/7, crusader 1101.[Ancestral Roots]
1 CONT
1 CONT ------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT The following post to SGM, 6 Mar 2003, by Thierry Stasser in responseto my query, dispells the marriage of Philippa & Sancho Ramirez, aswell as AR's "ca. 1073" birth date:
1 CONT
1 CONT From: Thierry Stasser (thierry.stasser@wanadoo.be)
1 CONT Subject: Re: Phillipa de Toulouse, granddaughter of Maud de Montgomery& Robert de Mortain
1 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval
1 CONT Date: 2003-03-06 12:42:53 PST
1 CONT
1 CONT William IV of Toulouse married Emma, dau of Robert of Mortain, beforeJune 16, 1080 (Histoire Générale de Languedoc, vol V, col 649- 652:ego Guillelmus Tolosanensium...comes et dux...me simul cum uxore meanomine Emma...facta carta 
1 CONC hujus donationis anno millesimo LXXXincarnationis Christi regnante Philippo rege...; and col 652-654: egoguillelmus dei gratia Tolosanorum ..;comes et dux et ego Emma uxoreius... facta carta donationis hujus anno Incarnatione Domi
1 CONC ni M LXXXregnante Philippo rege Francorum feria II , XVI kalendas julii...).William IV had been previously married to a lady Mantilis, mentionedin 1067 (Ibidem, vol V, col 544: ipse et Mantilis comitissa eiusuxor). William IV of T
1 CONC oulouse's second marriage is then dated1068/1080, but most probably about 1079, as Emma was not born before1064/1065.
1 CONT
1 CONT Contrary to previous assumptions, Philippa had not been married to theking of Aragon Sancho Ramirez (S de VAJAY, Ramire II le Moine, roid'Aragon et Agnes de poitou dans l'histoire et la légende, in Mélangesofferts à René crozet, 2
1 CONC  vol, Poitiers, 1966, vol 2, p 727-750; R EHarvey, The wives of the first troubadour Duke William IX ofAquitaine, in Journal of Medieval History, vol 19, 1993, p 315).Philippa married William IX of Aquitaine in 1094 (La chronique 
1 CONC deSaint Maixent, ed. J Verdon, Paris, 1979, p 170).  Sancho Ramirez ofAragon had been married 1st to Elisabeth of Urgell, and then by 1076to Felicia of Roucy (J de Salarrullana de Dios, Documentoscorrespondientes al reinado de San
1 CONC cho ramirez, Saragossa, 1907, vol 1,nr 12, p 25-26: ego Sancius gratia Dei rex et laudo hoc quod donavitregina domna Felicia mea    uxor...facta carta in era MCXIIII...; thisdocument is dated of Hispanic era). Queen Felicia was st
1 CONC ill alive injanuary 1094 (ibidem, vol I, nr 51, p 204-207: dono ego Sancius gratiaDei Aragonensium rex ...and ego felicia regina...facta carta eraMCXXXII...) and died on May 3, 1123 (Necrologio del monasterio de SanVictorian, in E
1 CONC spana sagrada, ed. H Florez, vol 46, p 278: V non. maiiobiit Felicia regina anno MCXXIII). King sancho ramirez died on June 61094. So he cannot have married Philippa of Toulouse
1 CONT
1 CONT I hope this helps
1 CONT
1 CONT Thierry
1 CONT
1 CONT dans l'article ab9770e6.0303050852.29109783@posting.google.com, JimWeber à
1 CONT jimweber@nwintl.com a écrit le 5/03/03 17:52 :
1 CONT
1 CONT > I ran into a problem with a date given by AR for the approximatebirth year of
1 CONT > Philippa de Toulouse, as it relates with the marriage dates givenfor her
1 CONT > parents and grandparents by CP.  I find that all of the datesinvolved are
1 CONT > questionable and could use the newsgroup's expertise in determiningthe better
1 CONT > dates.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > According to Weis' Ancestral Roots (AR), line 185-3, Phillipa (Maudor
1 CONT > Matilda), daughter of William IV de Toulouse and Emma de Mortain, m.(1)
1 CONT > Sancho Ramirez King of Aragon; (2) in 1094, William VII of Poitou &
1 CONT > Aquitaine.  The birth year "ca. 1073" given by AR for Philippa doesnot fit
1 CONT > with the marriage date given by CP for Emma's parents Robert deMortain & Maud
1 CONT > de Montgomery.  CP III:428 (Cornwall) states that Robert & Maud m."bef
1 CONT > 1066".  Nor does the 1073 date fit with marriage date given by CPfor the
1 CONT > parents of Maud de Montgomery: CP XI:686 (Shrewsbury) states thatRoger II de
1 CONT > Montgomery and Mabel, daughter of William Talvas d'Alencon, were
1 CONT > married "between 1050 and 1054".  For the latter marriage date, CPrefers to
1 CONT > White, "The First House of Belleme" in Trans. R. Hist. Soc., 4thSer., vol
1 CONT > xxii, pp. 67-99.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > The above dates lead to:
1 CONT >
1 CONT > 1. Roger II de Montgomery m. bet. 1050-1054, Mabel de Talvasd'Alencon.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > 2. Maud de Montgomery, b. 1050/4, m. bef. 1066, Robert de Mortain.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > 3. Emma de Mortain, b. c. 1066, m. William IV of Toulouse.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > 4. Philippa (Maud or Matilda) de Toulouse, b. c. 1073 (Ouch!)
1 CONT >
1 CONT > In the article on Hugh de Montgomery, son of Roger II & Mabel, CPXI:688
1 CONT > note "b" states that "According to a Welsh annalist, he [Hugh] wasfighting in
1 CONT > Wales in 1072 (Annales Cambriae, Rolls Ser., p. 26); but this seemsimpossibly
1 CONT > early."  I think that this implies that the birth of Hugh may havebeen
1 CONT > earlier than CP XI:688's "between 1053 and 1059", and that themarriage date
1 CONT > of Hugh's parents may have been earlier as well.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > As I stated above I think that both the birth date and the twomarriage dates
1 CONT > are off.  But I would appreciate any other sources that thenewsgroup could
1 CONT > use to determine what the appropriate dates might be.
1 CONT >
1 CONT > Jim Weber
1 CONT
1 CONT ---------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT The following e-mail from Peter Stewart, based on the above post toSGM, adds more info:
1 CONT
1 CONT Jim,
1 CONT
1 CONT In the article I mentioned Ruth Harvey discusses the evidence for whenPhilippa died, but not for the date of her birth.
1 CONT
1 CONT Here are some bits of information from other sources that may beuseful:
1 CONT
1 CONT The alleged marriage of Philippa to Sancho Ramirez of Aragon is false- there's no room for it chronologically, since he was married in 1076to Felicia de Roucy, who survived him & was not divorced. I suspectthis misunderstanding ca
1 CONC me about from the relationships of Sancho'sgranddaughter Petronilla, queen of Aragon, whose father was Sancho'sson Ramiro II, while her mother Agnes of Poitou was most likelyPhilippa's daughter.
1 CONT
1 CONT Philippa was definitely the daughter of her father's second wife, Emmade Mortain - there is a charter of hers in _Histoire général deLanguedoc_, vol V p 845: "Ego Philippa, Emae filia", leaving no doubton this point.
1 CONT
1 CONT Emma had been married to Guilhem IV, count of Toulouse before 16 June1080 when she appeared in two of his charters: "uxore mea nomineEmma", _HGL_ vol V p 649, and another of the same date on p 652.
1 CONT
1 CONT Philippa's marriage to Guilhem is firmly dated to 1094, according tothe chronicle of Saint-Maixent: "Anno MXCIIII...Guillelmus duxituxorem Philippam nomine, filiam Willelmi comitis Tholosani". She mayhave been already of child-bea
1 CONC ring age. Her eldest son was not bornuntil 1099, but it's recorded that she had daughters too and we don'tknow if one or more of them might have been born before him.
1 CONT
1 CONT Regards
1 CONT
1 CONT Peter
