1 CONC lliam. Founded the Benedictine Abbey of St. Peter and St. Paul Chatillon. He is said to have been the first to carry Norman arms to the Spainish Peninsula. He wassent to Spain by King Henry I of France to aide King Ferdinand. This
1 CONC  rough Normann leader was know for his cruely and invincibility. It was in Spain that hefound his wife. When William became the Duke of Normandy, Roger joined the revolt against him. But in a fight with Roger De Beaumont, both Rog
1 CONC er and his 2 sons, Herbert and Helmant, were killed.
