0 @N6000000001956363170@ NOTE
1 CONT Roger de Tony I "Hispanicus"
1 CONT Roger was born around 990 and died about 1040. The word 
1 CONT "Hispanicus" means "Spaniard", this is possibly because of his 
1 CONT involvement in the Spanish marches and also to distinguish him from 
1 CONT the other Rogers' de Tony involved in our Tony saga. We must remember 
1 CONT that he had joint custody of the Castle at Tillieres. Now with Ralph 
1 CONT his father gone to his reward, Roger has soul custody of the castle. 
1 CONT It has been said "that he was a powerful and haughty man."(2) He was 
1 CONT also the Hereditary Standard Bearer of all Normandy. Roger appears to 
1 CONT have inherited the fief of Toeni & Conches (known also as Chatillon) 
1 CONT that was situate to Evreux. He established the abbey of St. Peter and 
1 CONT St.Paul de Chatillon in the area of Conches. Conches hangs most 
1 CONT prominently on a hillside right above Rouloir, and there is a little 
1 CONT stream that flows into the Seine River. About the year 1030 Roger 
1 CONT attested a charter in the area of Wandrille, for Duke Robert I. Roger 
1 CONT while in Spain distinguished himself in fighting the Moors. Roger 
1 CONT also established a fortress in this area that is still evident to 
1 CONT this day. 
1 CONT The Church of St. Faith at Conches was a result of Roger's trip to 
1 CONT Spain to help the Christian princes in their fight against the Moors. 
1 CONT This all happened in the vicinity of the Pyrenean border area of 
1 CONT Spain. While in the Pyrenean area of Spain Roger met Godehildis, 
1 CONT daughter of Count Ramon Borel, and sister to Beranger Raymond. Ramon 
1 CONT Borel being the Count of Bacelona, who died fighting in a great 
1 CONT battle of the Cerdagne some years past. It is said that Count Ramon 
1 CONT was a good friend of Pope Sylvester II.
1 CONT
1 CONT Roger de Tony I in Spain
1 CONT As one might well imagine, a Norseman who takes a bride of The 
1 CONT House of Barcelona would be in for a surprise. Think of the 
1 CONT difference in the two cultures. The Tony family as with other 
1 CONT Norseman were fierce, known to be brutal and they were only recently 
1 CONT introduced to Christianity. As Constance Demaine Saunders has said, 
1 CONT "The Tonys and their kind had changed very little in nature since the 
1 CONT Raven banner floated over their dragon ships, between the fjords and 
1 CONT Iceland."(f) For the Barcelona family the most important 
1 CONT preoccupation for the past years had been -how to maintain 
1 CONT Christianity against the Islamic infiltrations. Many were to have 
1 CONT recurring nightmares of Moslem riders in white cloaks. 
1 CONT The parents of Lady Godehildis build a church and called it "The 
1 CONT Church of San Daniel de Gerona." This church build in the tenth 
1 CONT century, could have been where Roger and his bride married. After a 
1 CONT while the fighting has ceased and Roger makes a pilgrimage to 
1 CONT Santiago de Compostella, it having been recently recovered from the 
1 CONT Moors. He then took his bride and they both went to visit the Shrine 
1 CONT of St. Faith at Conques in Auvergne. It was a tradition to take 
1 CONT souvenirs of body parts of Saints. They chose the relics of the 
1 CONT Virgin Saint and took them home to Normandy. When they returned home 
1 CONT they dedicated the church that Roger had built near his home to the 
1 CONT Virgin who had died as a martyr at Agen in Dacian's persecution as 
1 CONT long as 700 years before.
1 CONT When Roger returned to Normandy he was furious, Duke Robert the 
1 CONT Magnificent had left for the Holy Land on a Crusade and had died 
1 CONT there. Now William, the illegitimate son of Robert would be the new 
1 CONT Norman ruler. Roger did something then that would prove the brutality 
1 CONT of his race. In about 1040 he ravaged the lands of his neighbors in 
1 CONT particular those of Humphrey de Vieilles. After this Humphrey's son 
1 CONT Roger de Beaumont of Pont Audemer retaliated on behalf of his family, 
1 CONT Roger de Tony and two of his sons were slain. He is buried in St. 
1 CONT Peter's Abbey in his hometown of Conches on May 30th, and that day 
1 CONT was observed for many years. Some say that he was buried in the 
1 CONT Chapter House under a marble slab that sits on the backs of three 
1 CONT stone lions. After Rogers's death Lady Godehildis marries Richard 
1 CONT Count of Evreux, grandson of Richard the Fearless, Duke of Normandy. 
1 CONT Godehildis had two children from this union. Their names are William 
1 CONT Count of Evreux and Agnes wife of Simon de Montfort, of whom we will 
1 CONT hear much more later.
1 CONT --The Toney Family book by Constance Demaine Saunders
