0 @N6000000003635725684@ NOTE [2438] WSHNGT.ASC file (Geo Washington Ahnentafel) # 4362670
0 @N6000000003949711863@ NOTE Styled also DE CONCHES, son and heir, was born probably about 990, for as stated above he was joined with his father in the custody of the castle of Tillières in 1013 or 1014. He was a powerful and haughty man, and banner-bearer o
1 CONC f all Normandy. In 1031 or 1032 he attested a charter of Robert I for St. Wandrille. About 1035 he founded the abbey of Chatillon or Conches. While Duke Robert was away on pilgrimage, he went to Spain and distinguished himself in 
1 CONC fighting the infidels (b). When he returned to Normandy, he was furious to learn that the boy William had succeeded his father in the Duchy, declaring that a bastard ought not to rule over him and other Normans. Accordingly he reb
1 CONC elled and ravaged the lands of his neighbours, particularly those of Humphrey de Vieilles; whose son Roger de Beaumont marched against him, and in the battle which followed Roger de Toeni and two of his sons were slain. He was a b
1 CONC enefactor to the abbey of I'Estrée and confirmed a gift to the abbey of Lire, and witnessed a charter for Jumièges. 
1 CONT However, if the Roger, son of Count Rodulf (cf, p. 755, note "a" above), who according to the Sens Chron. led an army from Normandy to Spain, can be identified with Roger de Toeni, he is said to have gone there at a much earlier d
1 CONC ate; and after defeating the Saracens, is said to have married a Spanish woman and lived there for 15 years. Then owing to the treachery of the natives he lost most of his men and, leaving his wife in Spain, he returned to Normand
1 CONC y; where he made a concord with Duke Richard, who was displeased at the loss of his army.   Lord of Guerny 
0 @N6000000004533082269@ NOTE Note: Roger Toeni's 1st wife, Stephanie, is questioned by some;especially her 2nd marriage to Garcias of Spain while Toeni was stillalive.  I agree that it does not make much sense.   However
1 CONT
1 CONT -------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT Roger de Toeni, also called Roger de Conches; fought Muslims in Spain;married 1st? Stephanie (m. 2nd Garsias, King of Spain) sister ofRaymond Berenger, Count of Barcelona; married 2nd? Godeheut (m. 2ndRichard, 3rd Count of Evreux)
1 CONC , and died 1038 or 1039 in battle againsta neighboring noble whose territory he had overrun in a revolt againstthe succession of William I the Conqueror to his father's Normanpossessions on the grounds that William was illegitimat
1 CONC e.  [Burke'sPeerage]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note:  According to BP, Roger married two different women as 1sthusband, both married later husbands.  There is no explanation given.Did the first marriage end in divorce?  As stated above, I am treatingthe women as the same perso
1 CONC n.
1 CONT
1 CONT ------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT ROGER DE TOENI I, styled also DE CONCHES, son and heir, was bornprobably about 990, for as stated above he was joined with his fatherin the custody of the castle of Tillières in 1013 or 1014. He was apowerful and haughty man, and 
1 CONC banner-bearer of all Normandy. In 1031or 1032 he attested a charter of Robert I for St. Wandrille. About1035 he founded the abbey of Chatillon or Conches. While Duke Robertwas away on pilgrimage, he went to Spain and distinguished
1 CONC  himself infighting the infidels (b). When he returned to Normandy, he wasfurious to learn that the boy William had succeeded his father in theDuchy, declaring that a bastard ought not to rule over him and otherNormans. Accordingl
1 CONC y he rebelled and ravaged the lands of hisneighbours, particularly those of Humphrey de Vieilles; whose sonRoger de Beaumont marched against him, and in the battle whichfollowed Roger de Toeni and two of his sons were slain. He wa
1 CONC s abenefactor to the abbey of I'Estrée and confirmed a gift to the abbeyof Lire, and witnessed a charter for Jumièges. He married, perhaps2ndly,[g] Godeheut, whose parentage is unknown. He died as above,probably in 1038 or 1039, a
1 CONC nd was buried 1 May at Conches. His widowmarried Richard, 3rd COUNT OF EVREUX. She was a benefactor to Conches.[Complete Peerage XII/1:755-7, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
1 CONT
1 CONT (b) Will. de Jumieges, p. 157---by Orderic.  In consequence he wasstyled sometimes Roger of Spain (Orderic, vol i, p. 180; vol iii, p.338), or Roger the Spaniard (Idem, vol ii, p. 64).  However, if theRoger, son of Count Rodulf (c
1 CONC f, p. 755, note "a" above), who accordingto the Sens Chron. led an army from Normandy to Spain, can beidentified with Roger de Toeni, he is said to have gone there at amuch earlier date; and after defeating the Saracens, is said t
1 CONC o havemarried a Spanish woman and lived there for 15 years.  Then owing tothe treachery of the natives he lost most of his men and, leaving hiswife in Spain, he returned to Normandy; where he made a concord withDuke Richard, who w
1 CONC as displeased at the loss of his army.  AfterwardsRoger was killed, fighting against a certain neighbor (Rec. des Hist.de France, vol x, p. 223).  This Roger's feats in Spain are recordedalso by Ademar, who calls him simply Roger,
1 CONC  and does not say how longhe stayed there (Idem, p. 156).  No other Norman than Roger de Toeniseems to be known, who could be identified with the hero of thesestories.  Cf. Prentout, op. cit., p. 86.  See also p. 755, note (a)abov
1 CONC e and note (g) below.  See "Tony of Belvoir", Charles Evans,"Geneal. Mag.", vol 15, 1968, pp. 616-18.  [last sentence, referencingCharles Evans, added by CP XIV:613]
1 CONT
1 CONT [g] Roger, son of Count Rodulf (see note "b" above), married, inSpain, Stephanie, sister of Raymond Berenger; which lady afterwards m.Garsias, King of Spain (Rec. des Hist. de France, vol x, p. 223). Thisagrees with the statement 
1 CONC of Ademar, that he m. a da. (unnamed) of thewidowed Ermensede, Countess of Barcelona ((Idem, p. 156), the motherof Raymond abovenamed. If this Roger were Roger de Toeni, he marriedGodeheut while his 1st wife was alive, and Stephan
1 CONC ie m. Garsias III,King of Navarre, while Roger was living.
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: The note "a", p. 755, referred to above is under Roger's father,Ralph.
