1 CONT GIVN Foulques V the Young of
1 CONT SURN Anjou
1 CONT Ruled Anjou jointly with his Father in 1106; succeeding as sole Count14 Apr 1109. Became Count of Maine by marriage 11 Jul 1110. He resigned Anjou and Maine to his eldest son and successor in 1129.
1 CONT  Hewas appointed Count of Tyre and Ptolmaide in 1129 and King of Jerusalem 21 Aug 1131; being crowned 14 Sep 1131. He was accidentally killed in the plain of Acre and was succeeded in Anjou and Maine
1 CONT  byGeoffrey.  [GADD.GED]
