1 CONT PAGE p 61The name Plantagenet, according to
1 CONT Rapin, came from when Fulk the Great being stung from remorse for some wicked
1 CONT action, in order to atone for it, went on a pilgrimage to Jerusalem, and was
1 CONT scourged before the Holy Sepulchre with broom twigs. Earlier authorities say
1 CONT it was because Geoffrey bore a branch of yellow broom (Planta-genistae) in
1 CONT his helm.
