0 @N6000000001783515029@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT Margaret Peverel (born c.1114) was a 12th century Countess of Derby , who lived at Tutbury Castle in the English county of Staffordshire.
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret was the daughter of William Peverel the Younger of Peveril Castle in Derbyshire and his wife, Avicia de Lancaster. Her grandfather was William Peverel.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT She married Robert Ferrers and thus became Countess of Derby. Their children were:
1 CONT William de Ferrers, 3rd Earl of Derby
1 CONT Walkelin de Derby
1 CONT Petronella
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Peverel>
