0 @N6000000005598882351@ NOTE Guillaume was styled as a very tall, broad, robust man with a hugh app etite.  He was very resentful of the way his father had treated hism o ther Philippa.  Guillaume's reign was troubled and brief marred by str ife with his vass
1 CONC els and quarrels with the church.  He patronised the troubadours Marcabru and Gascon Cercamon and he himself became known a s one of the first  troubadours.  Guillaume insured that his children received formal education - an excep
1 CONC tion for the time.  In about 1136 ,  Guillaume proposed to Emma, the daughter of Aymer of Limoges and wh o was the widow of the Lord Bardon de Cognac.  The marriage was howeve r prevented, when Emma was kidnapped the Count William
1 CONC  of Angouleme (W illiam IV 'Guillaume IV' de Taillefer) kidnapped and married Emma.  Th e instant Guillaume was involved with Geoffrey of Anjou in a move on N ormandie in support of Geoffrey's Matilda, in support of her claim to t
1 CONC he throne of England.  But the effort only lasted about four weeks. By this time, his vast domains included almost one-quarter of todays F rance, which included Poitou, Aquitaine and Gascony.  He made his daug hter Eleanor a ward 
1 CONC of his overlord Louis VI of France.  After his dea th, he was buried before the high altar next to the shrine of St. Jame s the Apostle.
1 CONT
