0 @N6000000002188182909@ NOTE Umayya ibn Abd Shams
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopediah
1 CONT
1 CONT Umayya ibn Abd Shams is whom the clan of Banu Umayyad is named after.
1 CONT
1 CONT Umayya was son of Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf, and the father of Harb ibn Umayya.
1 CONT
1 CONT However, the Shi'a Islam History claims that Umayya was not the real son of Abd-Shams, but that the latter, when visiting Rome, he saw a child being sold in miserable conditions. Being childless he adopted Ummaya and took him to A
1 CONC rabia where he was brought up. When Ummaya was young he departed from Quraish tribe [citation needed][original research?].
0 @N6000000002188182918@ NOTE Harb ibn Umayya
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Harb ibn Umayya was among the Sahaba's ancestors. Harb means "war".
1 CONT
1 CONT His father was Umayya ibn Abd Shams [1]
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the father of Harith ibn Harb and Abu Sufyan ibn Harb [2].
