0 @N6000000002187862893@ NOTE Conan III, Duke of Brittany
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Conan III of Cornwall (1070-1148) was duke of Brittany, from 1112 to his death. He was son of Duke Alan IV and Ermengarde of Anjou.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married before 1113 to Maud, an illegitimate daughter of King Henry I of England. By her he had three children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Constance of Brittany. 
1 CONT Bertha of Brittany, born circa 1114. Married Alan de Bretagne, 1st Earl of Richmond. 
1 CONT Hoel III. 
1 CONT On his deathbed he disinherited his only son, Hoel, for reason of illegitimacy.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Dukes of Brittany family tree 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Alan IV Duke of Brittany
1 CONT 1112–1148 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Hoel III and Eudes 
