0 @N6000000003300512970@ NOTE Married Henry I's daughter Matilda and had a son Henry who became Henry II
1 CONT Henry I arranged a marriage between his daughter Matilda and the son of Fulk V of Anjou, Geoffrey. He had previously arranged a marriage between his son William Audelin to Fulk's daughter also called Matilda, but William had died 
1 CONC in a ship wreck.
1 CONT Geoffrey was knighted by King Henry I on 10 June 1128, in Rouen.
1 CONT
1 CONT Geoffrey's habit of wearing a sprig of broom plant (planta genesta) in his hat is the origin of the name "Plantagenet."
