1 CONT Geoffrey V Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine was born on 24 August 1113. 
1 CONT He was the son of Fulk V d'Anjou, 9th Comte d'Anjou and 
1 CONT Aremburga de la Fleche, Comtesse de Maine.Cite2 
1 CONT He married Matilda 'the Empress' of England, daughter of Henry I 'Beauclerc', King of England and Editha of Scotland, on 22 May 1128 at Le Mans Cathedral, Le Mans, France.Cite3 He was also reported to have been married on 20 May 1
1 CONC 127. He died on 7 September 1151 at age 38 at Ch├óteau-du-Loir, France.Cite3 He was buried at Le Mans Cathedral, Le Mans, France.Cite3
1 CONT Geoffrey V Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine also went by the nick-name of Geoffrey 'the Fair'.1 He was also known as Geoffrey of Anjou.Cite4 He gained the title of 10th Comte d'Anjou in 1129.Cite3 He succeeded to the title of 1
1 CONC 2th Duc de Normandie on 19 January 1144.Cite3 He gained the title of Comte de Maine. He abdicated as Duke of Normandy in 1150.Cite1
1 CONT Child of Geoffrey V Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine
1 CONT * Mary of Shaftesbury d. c 1216 Cite2
1 CONT Child of Geoffrey V Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine and Adelaide of Angers
1 CONT * Hamelin d'Anjou, 5th Earl of Surrey+ b. c 1129, d. 7 May 1202 Cite2
1 CONT Children of Geoffrey V Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine and Matilda 'the Empress' of England
1 CONT * Emma Plantagenet d. b 1214 Cite2
1 CONT * Henry II 'Curtmantle' d'Anjou, King of England+ b. 5 Mar 1133, d. 6 Jul 1189
1 CONT * Geoffrey VI d'Anjou, Comte d'Anjou et Nantes b. 1 Jun 1134, d. 26 Jul 1158
1 CONT * William de Poitou, Comte de Poitou b. c Jul 1136, d. 30 Jan 1164
