1 CONC f Henry I 'Beauclerc', King of England and Editha of Scotland, on 22 May 1128 at Le Mans Cathedral, Le Mans, France.3 He was also reported to have been married on 20 May 1127. He died on 7 September 1151 at age 38 at Château-du-Lo
1 CONC ir, France.3 He was buried at Le Mans Cathedral, Le Mans, France.3
1 CONT      Geoffrey V Plantagenet, Comte d'Anjou et Maine also went by the nick-name of Geoffrey 'the Fair'.1 He was also known as Geoffrey of Anjou.4 He gained the title of 10th Comte d'Anjou in 1129.3 He succeeded to the title of 12th
1 CONC  Duc de Normandie on 19 January 1144.3 He gained the title of Comte de Maine. He abdicated as Duke of Normandy in 1150.1
