0 @N6000000002187750165@ NOTE Alfonso II, Count of Provence
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Alfonso II (died 1209) was the second son of Alfonso II of Aragon and Sancha of Castile. His father transferred the County of Provence from his uncle Sancho to him in 1185.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1193, Alfonso married Gersenda II of Sabran, daughter of Rainou, Count of Forcalquier and Gersend of Forcalquier. They had a child who became Ramon Berenguer IV as count of Provence.
1 CONT
1 CONT According to explanations in the manuscripts of Gaucelm Faidit's poems, Alfonso was a rival of the troubadour's for the love of Jourdaine d'Embrun.[1]
1 CONT
1 CONT Alfonso II died in Palermo, Sicily, Italy.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Notes
1 CONT ^ Biographies des troubadours ed. J. Boutière, A.-H. Schutz (Paris: Nizet, 1964) pp. 187-191.  
