1 CONT A controversy with Pope Innocent II over Louis's refusal to accept th e papal appointee to the archbishopric of Bourges led to a papal inter dict on Louis and to warfare between the king and the count of Champag ne, who supported 
1 CONC the papal candidate. It was settled, after the inter vention of St. Bernard of Clairvaux, by Louis's capitulation (1144) t o Pope CelestineII, Innocent's successor. In the course of that war Ge offrey IV (Geoffrey Plantagenet), co
1 CONC unt of Anjou, completed his conque st of Normandie; Louis, in return for a small concession, acquiesced i n the conquest.  This brought the interdict upon the King's lands.
