0 @N6000000008176865107@ NOTE [howard.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis VII, called The Young (1121?-80), king of France (1137-80), son and successor of Louis VI. In the first year of his reign he married Eleanor of Aquitaine, daughter of William X, duke of Aquitaine. Louis soon aroused the oppo
1 CONC sition of Pope Innocent II because of his support of a rival to the papal candidate for the archbishopric of Bourges, and his lands were placed under papal interdict. Louis next fought a 2-year war and conquered Champagne in 1144.
1 CONC  In 1147 he joined the unsuccessful Second Crusade as one of its two chief military leaders (the other was Conrad III of Germany). Louis returned to France two years later, and in 1152 his marriage to Eleanor was annulled; in the 
1 CONC same year she married Henry of Anjou, later Henry II, king of England. Louis warred with Henry for the possession of Aquitaine but renounced all rights to the duchy in 1154, the year Henry became king of England. Between 1157 and 
1 CONC 1180 Louis continued sporadic warfare against Henry, who held many of the French provinces. Louis was succeeded by his son Philip II (Philip Augustus).
1 CONT "Louis VII," Microsoft (R) Encarta. Copyright (c) 1994 Microsoft Corporation. Copyright (c) 1994 Funk & Wagnall's Corporation.
0 @N6000000007329573866@ NOTE [Kopi av ROYALS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis was succeded by his son Philip II (Philip Augustus)[Chambers Bio.] Louis VII reigned from 1137. Married to Eleanor of
1 CONT Aquitane, marriage annuled, she later married Henry II of England.
1 CONT [sawnson -at- butler.edu]: Expert historians who have an intimate
1 CONT knowledge  of the source material often describe Alice as the daughter of
1 CONT Louis   VII and  Constance of Castile. (For example, W. L. Warren, Henry
1 CONT II,  and John   Baldwin,  The Government of Philip Augustus.)  Experts in
1 CONT medieval  genealogy   tend to  describe her as the daughter of Louis VII
1 CONT and Adela of  Champagne.   (For  example, Europaische Stammtafeln (1984
1 CONT ed) Table 11.) I'd  be   grateful to know  if any readers of this list
1 CONT know of primary source  material which   might help  resolve the question
1 CONT one way or another. Scott  Swanson. DATE  Date   Unknown  QUAY 0
1 CONT Person Source
