1 CONC  turned over to Robert of Neubourg, chief Justice of Normandie, who held a castle on the French border.  In 1160, she wa s brought forward at the command of Henry II to Rouen and there marrie d to Henry 'the Young King'.  At the t
1 CONC ime of her husband's death, it i s reported that she was involved in an affair with William 'the protec tor' Marshall.  In December of 1183, Margarets half-brother Phillippe met with Henry II of England, and Henry II agreed to pay
1 CONC  Margaret an a nnual pension.  After the death of her second husband Bela in 1196, Ma rgaret made a pilgrimage to the Holy Land.
